{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat collab/yang-base/1795198164100-architect-yang-preludes-design-r4-jupiter.gpt-6.2-astra.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-20 18:17:14 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-21 01:17:14 +07 (+0700)\nCoding-Agent: codex\nHost: jupiter.stigmergy.systems (Codex Pool 2)\nSession-ID: 01a1fa26-9e21-79a2-bb32-f1b87e22212c\n# Task: Architecture review r4 confirmation of docs/design/yang.preludes.md (all 13 r3 findings reconciled; fresh Pool-2 session)\nRole: Lead System Architect\nImplementers:\n- Model: gpt-6.2-astra | Assigned: 2026-11-21 01:09:24 +07 (+0700) | Status: completed | Rationale: Independent OpenAI GPT-6.2 flagship Lead System Architect review on jupiter.stigmergy.systems (Codex Pool 2 failover after Pool-1 quota exhaustion in 1795197640465)\n\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-20 18:14:50 GMT  \nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-20 13:14:50 EST (-0500)\n\n## 1. Verdict\n\n**`REVISE` — 6 of 13 r3 findings are `CONFIRMED-FIXED`.** The numeric corrections, callable predicate, host-limit input, and comprehension accumulator contract resolve their reported defects. Three issues independently block P3 sign-off: the provenance rule rejects the proposed dependency graph, the linked export accessor resolves its own lookup incorrectly, and the admitted key domain still permits host-dependent data loss. P0 also has an emission rule that conflicts with its byte-parity gate.\n\nI reviewed the full 794-line working-tree design at `9cf135c2`, the prior reviews, and the referenced source and specification contracts. I checked the floor-division, negative-power, and rounding witnesses with in-memory arithmetic. **No files were edited.** Repository suites and four-host acceptance gates were not run.\n\n## 2. r3 finding-by-finding disposition\n\nLine numbers in this table refer to [docs/design/yang.preludes.md](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md).\n\n| r3 | Disposition | Line and code evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| #1 Float and mixed arithmetic | `CONFIRMED-FIXED` | Lines 564–582 specify promotion, arithmetic, zero-divisor handling, unary signs, signed-zero quotients, and the rounding correction. The finite branch matches `python/antlr/prelude.cljc:1427–1437`. I reproduced `2.1 // 0.7 → 3.0` and both signed-zero witnesses. |\n| #2 Integer refusals before use | `CONFIRMED-FIXED` | Lines 558–562, 584–589, and 679 check pair results before indexing, guard `from-float` before `compare-float`, unwrap mixed comparisons, and check `neg`. These match the result shapes in `yin/vm/integer.cljc:178`, `:285`, and `:454`. |\n| #3 Portable keys and recursive equality | `OPEN` | Lines 592–604 cover nested floats and lists, including NaN in map values. They also admit all keywords and symbols and use host equality for them. Jing documents a concrete identifier pair that collapses on Node at `dao.jing.cbor.md:266`. |\n| #4 Callable predicate and emitter syntax | `CONFIRMED-FIXED` | Lines 640–653 and 682 use nested `if` and share one admission predicate across `fn?` and dynamic calls. `yang/core/uast.cljc:88–101` emits those forms directly. |\n| #5 Invocation-record validation | `OPEN` | Lines 658–664 put all four checks in the correct order and preserve ordinary binding errors under `:yang.call/thrown`. The executable forms at 659–660 construct the wrong condition evidence under the designated emitter. |\n| #6 Linker exports and task-local cells | `OPEN` | Lines 693–703 separate installation from task initialization and provide trusted traversal entries. At line 697, the stripped module’s bare `get` resolves to its public zero-argument `get` accessor. The VM searches the module store before primitives. |\n| #7 Trusted bridge and shared context | `OPEN` | Lines 72 and 633–636 establish the shared Clojure exception domain and both emitters. Lines 303 and 673 together prohibit the derived footprint of the required bridge consumer. The legacy emitter also retains its own provenance calls. |\n| #8 Four-host `clojure.core` surface | `OPEN` | Lines 684–687 address counters, float text, traversal, and indices. The comparator lacks rules for admitted same-kind compound keys and absent namespaces. The retained `sequential?` also changes meaning when paired with the new `map?`. |\n| #9 Executable descriptor validation | `OPEN` | Lines 483–489 now cover hooks, literal calls, optional `:comp/finish`, and projections in the selected closure. The specified inputs establish export-name membership. Schema 1 supplies no guest export arity or accessor-role evidence. |\n| #10 Admission inputs and dependency edges | `CONFIRMED-FIXED` | Lines 294–298 distinguish direct root pins from the transitive walk. Lines 306–308 give `admit-profile` the trusted `host-limits` input required by the registration model in `yin/vm/module.cljc:249` and `python/antlr/prelude.cljc:4163`. |\n| #11 Negative-power witnesses and phase placement | `CONFIRMED-FIXED` | Lines 184, 543–546, and 765 place `data/float64?` in P3. The P1 gate distinguishes denominator underflow for `0.5 ** -2000`, the minimum subnormal for `2.0 ** -1074`, and positive zero for `2.0 ** -2000`, consistent with `python/antlr/prelude.cljc:1530–1543`. |\n| #12 Bare `except:` and eager comprehensions | `CONFIRMED-FIXED` | Lines 374–376 match `Python3Parser.g4:313–315`. Lines 415–421 and 621–624 define accumulator creation, mutation, and finish for all three eager kinds. A nil default finish preserves the existing return of `acc` at `python/antlr/lower.cljc:2334–2339`. |\n| #13 Effect example and D7 names | `OPEN` | Line 793 fixes both `-raw` names. Line 286 still omits `:module/require` from the illustrative Python ceiling. The linked Python tree explicitly evaluates `require` at `python/antlr/prelude.cljc:4112`. |\n\n**Earlier closures.** The design retains r1 **#2** frontend ownership and structural lowering (334–338, 608–625), **#5** open generator frames and language-specific restoration (143–155, 232), **#8** the integer refusal algebra (217–226), and **#9** the recipe/root-pin distinction (269–298). For r1 **#10**, the phase boundaries and independent P1 validation remain intact, but the P0 parity claim has the concrete exception below.\n\nThe r2 corrections also remain present: **F2** protects binding and preserves normal returns (661–664), **F5** requires identity-preserving construction for dynamically returned functions (700–703), **F6** uses qualified frame reads (151), **F7** keeps policy callbacks outside raw-float frames (187–190), and **F8** keeps both active ceilings `nil` (266, 286). F5 depends on the constructor repair below. F8 remains closed despite the error in the optional example.\n\n## 3. New or remaining findings\n\n| Severity | File:line | Invariant / evidence | Recommended correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **HIGH** | [yang.preludes.md:303](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:303) | Publication unions every dependency’s effects into `:yin.module/footprint`. Because `clojure.core` requires `clj.bridge`, its footprint necessarily contains the two provenance effects. The proposed admission check therefore rejects a correctly constructed library. Also, “all Clojure-family” ownership at line 634 conflicts with P3 byte parity: existing Clojure-generated entries and callers emit provenance operations directly. [Footprint derivation](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:81) · [Existing entry](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1250) · [Existing caller](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1448) | Enforce the door restriction on each module’s **direct** primitive declarations and exports. Use the transitive footprint for the profile ceiling. Scope P3 bridge ownership to the new consumers and identify the legacy migration separately. |\n| **HIGH** | [yang.preludes.md:697](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:697) | In linked mode, `clojure.core/get` becomes the store key `get`. The displayed `(get (cell/get clojure.core.rt/exports) sym)` therefore calls the zero-argument accessor, which calls `export` again. Yin drops surplus closure arguments, so this can recurse instead of looking up even `identity`. The same collision affects primitive wrappers that use their public bare names internally. [Namespace stripping](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc:42) · [Resolution order](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:116) · [Closure argument binding](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:56) | Give primitive implementations a collision-free qualified path, such as a separately pinned guest adapter module. Exercise linked `(clojure.core/identity)` and `(clojure.core/get)` through initialization, lookup, and invocation. |\n| **HIGH** | [yang.preludes.md:656](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:656) | `entry` must close over `owner`, but the displayed `cell/new` expects that entry before it returns `owner`. Separately, the maps at lines 659–660 contain `owner` and a `get` expression. `sexp->uast` emits an entire map as a literal, so the condition carries syntax where runtime evidence is required. [Emitter](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc:82) · [Working two-step constructor](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:944) | Allocate the owner cell, install the entry closing over that cell with `cell/set!`, then expose it. Build condition evidence with evaluated `assoc` calls. Assert the actual owner and supplied binding-profile value at the raise exit. |\n| **HIGH** | [yang.preludes.md:593](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:593) | `(keyword nil \"a/b\")` and `(keyword \"a\" \"b\")` both pass `admit-key!`. They have distinct Jing identities, but CLJS can merge them in a host map or set. The same issue applies to symbols, nested keys, and the host `=` fallback at line 604. Post-construction scanning cannot restore a lost entry. [Jing’s documented host-collapse case](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md:266) | Compare identifiers by kind, namespace, and name. Adopt a recursively enforced, unambiguous identifier domain for v1 keys, or use field-based storage keys. Gate construction, lookup, scalar equality, and a nested-vector case with this exact pair. |\n| **HIGH** | [yang.preludes.md:487](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:487) | The frontend table at line 335 describes expected hook arity. The artifact store at line 295 supplies manifests. Their `:yin.module/exports` is a set of names, so these inputs cannot distinguish a zero-argument accessor from a same-named unary function, establish a `:value` export’s kind, or establish initializer behavior. [Published schema](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:375) | Bind trusted export roles and signatures to the exact module address, or derive structural facts from its verified UAST. Establish behavioral promises such as idempotence through conformance of that pinned artifact. Reject a selected module with the correct export name and wrong role or arity. |\n| **HIGH** | [yang.preludes.md:310](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:310) | P0 cannot derive one executable `require` per dependency and preserve existing trees. Both `clj` and `js` pin `yang.call` but emit no trailing `require`. Python emits one, and its live module emitter also lacks the C1 finalization asserted at line 310. Adding a `require` changes canonical rows; adding C1 marks changes the side table. [Clojure emitter and spec](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:183) · [JS emitter](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:4371) · [Python emitter](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:4105) | Represent direct dependency pins, emitted trailing forms, and C1 finalization independently in each recipe. Freeze both the emitted tree and the side-table result for each existing emitter. |\n| **HIGH** | [yang.preludes.md:613](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:613) | The descriptor owns ambient projections, yet `global-get` receives only `[globals-cell name]`. Line 625 initializes the cell to `{}`. Two descriptors can pin the same `clj.py` address and select different aliases. On a global miss, the runtime has no specified input that distinguishes their tables. | Carry the descriptor-selected resolver in the compiled unit’s environment, or require a separately pinned adapter specialized to that projection table. Gate two units in one task that map the same alias to different exports. |\n| **MEDIUM** | [yang.preludes.md:676](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:676) | The retained `sequential?` means `coll?` and neither `map?` nor `set?`. An authenticated cell is represented by a host map. Once the new `map?` excludes it, the retained predicates classify it as sequential and as a list. Line 686 also leaves within-kind vector/map/set comparison unspecified and sends a possibly nil namespace to string-only `data/str-compare`. The P3 gate lists `[NaN] == [NaN]` among “accepting” cases without specifying its required false result. [Retained predicates](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2743) · [String comparator](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc:396) | Classify authenticated handles before collection dispatch. Define absent-namespace ordering and recursive lexicographic rules. Pin exact ordered outputs and explicitly assert `[NaN] == [NaN] → false`. |\n| **LOW** | [yang.preludes.md:286](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:286) | The example enumerates six **cell** effects. The linked `py` tree also invokes `require`, whose primitive profile declares `:module/require`. A ceiling copied from the example rejects Python under line 305. [Python trailing form](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:4112) · [Primitive effect](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:429) | Derive the illustrative ceiling from the published footprint, or include `:module/require` and test that the displayed set admits the linked recipe. |\n\n## 4. Owner-decision confirmation\n\nAll seven questions remain suitable for owner disposition. The outstanding findings affect the conditions attached to D4–D6. [Owner decision text](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:772)\n\n| Decision | Architectural recommendation |\n|---|---|\n| D1 | **A.** Use task-local lexical cells for reassignment and `nonlocal`. Keep single assignment as a distinct profile. |\n| D2 | **A.** Use `yrt.*` linker names and `yang.rt.*` implementation namespaces. |\n| D3 | **A.** Retain Python’s float tag through P1. |\n| D4 | **Conditional A.** Establish the exact P0 baseline, validate each extraction independently, then coordinate activation. |\n| D5 | **A.** Curate aliases with lexical precedence. Bind each unit’s projections and each target’s ABI to verified artifacts. |\n| D6 | **Constrained A.** Keep default Clojure bundling unchanged in P3. Standalone publication requires the provenance, accessor, constructor, and portability corrections above. |\n| D7 | **A for P1.** The two `-raw` names are consistent. The `1.1 ** 6` witness reproduces `0x1.c585058dde7acp+0` for half-power squaring and `0x1.c585058dde7abp+0` for base squaring. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
