{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '523,698p'\"","aggregated_output":"   523\t## 7. Case study: `yang.python` with a `clojure.core` prelude (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`)\n   524\t\n   525\tThis section specifies the reference cross-paradigm profile in full, reconciling Python's lowering ABI, 4-host numeric portability, cross-unit callable admission, §8.10.7 exception bridging, and a portable `clojure.core` module.\n   526\t\n   527\t### 7.1 Value representation & semantic mapping\n   528\t\n   529\t| Python syntax | Native `py` prelude (`:yang.python/py-v1`) | `clojure.core` prelude (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`) |\n   530\t|---|---|---|\n   531\t| `None` | `:py/None` | `nil` |\n   532\t| `True` / `False` | `true` / `false` (numeric as `1`/`0`) | `true` / `false` (**non-numeric**: arithmetic raises guest error) |\n   533\t| `\"abc\"` | `{:py/str \"abc\"}` | `\"abc\"` (raw Yin/UTF-8 string) |\n   534\t| `42` | exact integer (safe raw, else `py/int-lit`) | exact integer (safe raw, else `clj.py/int-lit`) |\n   535\t| `1.5` | `{:py/float <float64>}` | `<float64>` (untagged Jing `data/float64` carrier) |\n   536\t| `[1, 2]` | cell `{:py/type :list :items [1 2]}` | persistent vector `[1 2]` |\n   537\t| `(1, 2)` | `{:py/type :tuple :items [1 2]}` | persistent vector `[1 2]` |\n   538\t| `{\"a\": 1}` | cell `{:py/type :dict ...}` | persistent map `{\"a\" 1}` |\n   539\t| `{1, 2}` | cell `{:py/type :set ...}` | persistent set `#{1 2}` |\n   540\t| `def f(x): ...` | cell `{:py/type :function :code (fn [args] ...) :yang.call/entry ...}` | authenticated cell `{:clj.py/type :function :name s :spec spec :yang.call/entry ...}` |\n   541\t| Truthiness | `0`, `\"\"`, `[]`, `{}`, `None`, `False` falsy | Clojure truthiness (`clj.py/truthy`): only `nil` and `false` falsy (`0`, `\"\"`, `[]` are truthy) |\n   542\t| Equality `==` / `!=` | `1 == 1.0 == True`, structural list/dict | Recursive kind-strict equality (`clj.py/eq`): `1 == 1` `true`, `1 == 1.0` `false`, `1 == True` `false`, `NaN == NaN` `false`, `0.0 == -0.0` `true`, recursive over persistent collections |\n   543\t\n   544\t*Truth-in-advertising invariant:* `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` explicitly declares Clojure truthiness, persistent immutable collections, non-numeric booleans, and kind-strict equality as its support profile — never CPython parity.\n   545\t\n   546\t### 7.2 Portable numeric & collection contract (`clj.py` over `yin.vm.integer` + `yrt.float` + `yrt.int`)\n   547\t\n   548\tPer `yang.antlr.md` §8.5.5, raw `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=` on decoded `data/float64` carriers are **not portable across Node/JVM/Dart**. Furthermore, `yin.vm.data/data-number?` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc:418`) recognizes host numbers and exact-integer carriers, **not** CLJS `Float64` carriers (`src/cljc/dao/host/number.cljc:76`).\n   549\t\n   550\t**P3 Host prerequisites (`data/float64?` and `kind/namespace`):**\n   551\t1. **`data/float64?`** (`src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc`): one `:pure` unary export backed directly by existing `dao.jing.cbor/float64?` (`src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:212` — already implemented for JVM `Double`/`Float`, Dart `double`, JS `Float64`/non-integral/non-finite/`-0.0` `Number`, and Jolt Scheme flonums).\n   552\t2. **`kind/namespace`** (`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2578`, `:kind-module` / `:kind-arities`): one `:pure` unary export backed by `namespace`, enabling standalone `clojure.core` (`§7.5`) to sort and render namespaced symbols and keywords deterministically without host `kind/str`.\n   553\tLike owner decision A12.6 in `yang.typescript.md`, adding these two pure host exports changes no existing `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj` manifest or golden address; both are explicit prerequisites of P3 and are not needed in P1.\n   554\t\n   555\tTherefore, `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` routes ALL arithmetic, floor division, remainder, power, comparisons, and equality through `clj.py/*` adapters requiring host `integer` (`:min-bits 53`) and `data` (with `data/float64?`):\n   556\t\n   557\t1. **Portable kind classification (`clj.py/num-kind`):**\n   558\t   ```clojure\n   559\t   (if (integer/integer? x)\n   560\t     :int\n   561\t     (if (data/float64? x) :float :other))\n   562\t   ```\n   563\t   `true`/`false`, `nil`, strings, symbols, keywords, collections, callables, and cells all answer `:other` cleanly across all four hosts (`integer/integer?` at `src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc:595`). Non-numeric operands raise guest error `{:clj.py/error :type-error ...}` (in `v1`, string `+` concatenates via `data/str-concat`; `*` is strictly numeric).\n   564\t2. **Int × Int (universal `yrt.int/check-limit` gate):**\n   565\t   - **Every** `integer/*` operation returning through `yin.vm.integer`'s `out` / `pair` contract (`add`, `sub`, `neg`, `mul`, `floor-div-mod`, `quot-rem`, `pow`, `to-float`, `true-div`, `from-float`, `format` — including **`integer/neg`** on externally supplied exact operands!) MUST pass through `yrt.int/check-limit` **before** indexing a `[q r]` pair via `data/nth` or forwarding a result into any subsequent `integer/*` or `yrt.float/*` primitive. Any `:yin.vm.integer/bit-limit`, `:digit-limit`, or `:float-overflow` reason translates to a guest error map via `clj/raise`; operational host throws are never caught.\n   566\t   - `+`, `-`, `*`, `//`, `%`, `**` (`e >= 0`), `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`: check `b == 0` **before** `integer/floor-div-mod` or `integer/true-div` (raising guest zero-division error rather than an operational throw); filter `floor-div-mod` through `yrt.int/check-limit` before calling `data/nth` for `//` or `%`.\n   567\t   - `/`: checks `b != 0`, calls `(yrt.int/check-limit (integer/true-div a b) ...)`, and boxes via `data/float64`.\n   568\t   - `**` with negative integer exponent `e < 0`: if `a == 0` raises guest zero-division error; otherwise computes `base-boxed = (data/float64 (yrt.int/check-limit (integer/to-float a) ...))` and `pos-e = (yrt.int/check-limit (integer/neg e) ...)`, and calls `(yrt.float/neg-pow-result base-boxed pos-e :half)`. If `yrt.float/neg-pow-result` returns `:yrt.float/underflow`, `clj.py` raises guest overflow error `{:clj.py/error :overflow ...}` outside any raw-double leaf frame.\n   569\t   - Unary `-` (`clj.py/neg`) / `+` (`clj.py/pos`): unary `-` computes `(yrt.int/check-limit (integer/neg a) ...)`; unary `+` returns `a` unchanged.\n   570\t3. **Float × Float and Mixed Int × Float:**\n   571\t   - Exact int operands promote via `(data/float64 (yrt.int/check-limit (integer/to-float i) ...))`.\n   572\t   - **`+`, `-`, `*`:** Unwrap both boxed floats via `data/float-value` inside pure leaf helpers, evaluate IEEE-754 double `+`, `-`, `*`, and rebox via `data/float64` (producing IEEE `±Inf`/`NaN` on overflow/invalid results).\n   573\t   - **`/` (`clj.py/truediv`):** Unwraps boxed `y` in a pure leaf helper to check `(yrt.float/zero? y)` **first** and raises guest zero-division error `{:clj.py/error :zero-division :op :truediv}` (consistent with Int × Int `/`, `//`, and `%`); for nonzero `y`, delegates boxed operands to `yrt.float/fdiv` (returning boxed `data/float64`, including IEEE `±Inf`/`NaN` on `x = ±Inf` / `NaN` / finite overflow).\n   574\t   - **Unary `-` and `+` on `:float`:** Unary `-` unwraps `x` in a pure leaf helper and returns `(data/float64 (* (data/float-value -1) x))` (preserving signed zero `-0.0 ↔ +0.0` across CLJD/JVM/CLJS/Jolt, never `(- 0 x)`); unary `+` returns the boxed `data/float64` unchanged.\n   575\t   - **`//` (`clj.py/float-floordiv`):**\n   576\t     - Zero divisor (`y == 0.0`): raises guest zero-division error `{:clj.py/error :zero-division :op :floordiv}`.\n   577\t     - `NaN` in either operand, or non-finite `x` (`±Inf`): returns boxed `yrt.float/nan` (matching `py/float-divmod:1426`).\n   578\t     - Finite `x`, infinite `y` (`±Inf`): handled directly in a leaf helper — if `x == 0.0` returns `(data/float64 (* (data/float-value 0) (/ x y)))` (preserving signed zero); if `x != 0.0` and signs differ returns `(data/float64 -1)`, else `(data/float64 0)`.\n   579\t     - Finite `x`, finite nonzero `y`: inside pure leaf helper `clj.py/float-floordiv-raw [x y]`, mirrors `py/float-divmod` (`src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:1427–1437`):\n   580\t       - `m0 = (yrt.float/fmod-pos (yrt.float/abs x) (yrt.float/abs y))`, `m = (if (< x 0) (- 0 m0) m0)`\n   581\t       - `adjust = (if (yrt.float/zero? m) false (not (= (< y 0) (< m 0))))`\n   582\t       - `div = (- (/ (- x m) y) (data/float-value (if adjust 1 0)))`\n   583\t       - **Signed-zero quotient branch:** `(if (yrt.float/zero? div) (* (data/float-value 0) (/ x y)) ...)` — preserves `-0.0 // 2.0 -> -0.0` and `0.0 // -2.0 -> -0.0`.\n   584\t       - **Quotient rounding correction:** `(let [f (yrt.float/float-floor-raw div)] (if (< (data/float-value 0.5) (- div f)) (+ f (data/float-value 1)) f))` — ensures `2.1 // 0.7` (whose intermediate `div` is `2.9999999999999996`, flooring to `2.0`) evaluates to **`3.0`** while non-finite or `>= 2^53` quotients pass through unchanged; result is boxed via `data/float64`.\n   585\t   - **`%` (`clj.py/float-mod`):** guards ALL preconditions before ever reaching `yrt.float/fmod-pos`:\n   586\t     - Zero divisor (`y == 0.0`): raises guest zero-division error.\n   587\t     - `NaN` in either operand, or non-finite `x` (`±Inf`): returns boxed `yrt.float/nan`.\n   588\t     - Finite `x`, infinite `y` (`±Inf`): handled directly without `fmod-pos` — returns `zero-like(y)` when `x == 0.0`, `x` when `x` and `y` share sign, and `y` (`±Inf`) when signs oppose (floored modulo).\n   589\t     - Finite `x`, finite nonzero `y`: calls `m0 = (yrt.float/fmod-pos (abs x) (abs y))` inside a pure leaf frame, restores dividend sign `m`, converts `m == 0.0` to `zero-like(y)`, sign-corrects `m` toward `y`, and returns `data/float64`.\n   590\t   - **`**` (`clj.py/float-pow` — strict leaf unwrap + limit check before compare):**\n   591\t     - Pure leaf helper `clj.py/float-exp-info [y-boxed]` unwraps `y = (data/float-value y-boxed)` (so `yin.vm.integer/float!` receives a native unwrapped `host-float?` on all 4 hosts, including CLJS!):\n   592\t       - Returns `:zero` when `(yrt.float/zero? y)`, `:nan` when `(yrt.float/nan? y)`, `:infinite` when `(not (yrt.float/finite? y))`;\n   593\t       - Otherwise (finite nonzero `y`), binds `e = (integer/from-float y)` and **checks `(integer/integer? e)` BEFORE calling `(integer/compare-float e y)`**! If `e` is a limit keyword (e.g., `:yin.vm.integer/bit-limit` for `2.0 ** 53` at `:max-bits 53`), returns that keyword immediately out of the leaf frame (never passing `:yin.vm.integer/bit-limit` into `integer/compare-float`); otherwise checks `(= (integer/compare-float e y) 0)` and returns exact integer `e` or `:fractional`.\n   594\t     - Outer wrapper `clj.py/float-pow` (with no raw double live!) handles `:zero -> (data/float64 1)` (even for `NaN ** 0.0`), `:nan -> (yrt.float/nan)`, `:infinite -> guest :pow-infinite`, `:fractional -> guest :pow-fractional`, and translates limit reasons via `yrt.int/check-limit`.\n   595\t     - For exact integral `e`: checks `x` NaN via pure leaf unwrap (`-> (yrt.float/nan)`); for `e >= 0`, evaluates `yrt.float/fpow-half-raw` inside a pure leaf helper and boxes via `data/float64`; for `e < 0`, checks `x == 0.0` (`-> guest :zero-division`), computes `pos-e = (yrt.int/check-limit (integer/neg e) ...)`, and calls `(yrt.float/neg-pow-result x-boxed pos-e :half)` (translating `:yrt.float/underflow` to guest `:overflow` outside the leaf frame).\n   596\t   - **Mixed ordering (`<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`):** Float × Float unwraps both via `data/float-value` inside a pure leaf helper; Int × Float / Float × Int unwraps the boxed float via `data/float-value` inside a pure leaf helper, returns `false` if `(yrt.float/nan? f)`, and calls `integer/compare-float` strictly on the unwrapped non-NaN host double (never passing a boxed CLJS `Float64` or `NaN` to `integer/compare-float` and never rounding large integers to float).\n   597\t4. **Uniform portable key/element domain (`admit-key!`) & recursive equality (`clj.py/eq`, `clj.py/ne`):**\n   598\t   - **Why a uniform key/element gate is required (`yin/vm/data.cljc:34–36`, `dao.jing.cbor.md:173, 266`):** Host map/set hashing and Jing canonical CBOR encoding cannot recover distinct keys once collapsed by host collection construction (`1` vs `1.0`, `[[-0.0]]`, `NaN`, OR `(keyword nil \"a/b\")` vs. `(keyword \"a\" \"b\")` on CLJS), and host map/set lookup diverges across JVM (`1 != 1.0`) vs JS (`1 == 1.0` and joined keyword strings).\n   599\t   - **One uniform `v1` portable key/element admission gate (`admit-key!`):** Enforced across BOTH `clj.py` (`map-from`, `set-from`, `get-item`, `comp-set-add`, `comp-dict-set`) AND `clojure.core.impl` (`impl-assoc`, `impl-assoc-in`, `impl-update`, `impl-update-in`, `impl-get`, `impl-get-in`, `impl-contains?`, `impl-conj` on maps/sets, `impl-disj`, `impl-merge`, `impl-into` targeting maps/sets, `impl-union`, `impl-difference`, `impl-hash-map`, `impl-set`, `impl-get-coll`, `impl-assoc-coll`, `impl-conj-coll`):\n   600\t     - **Admitted keys / set elements (recursively):**\n   601\t       - `nil`, booleans, exact integers (`integer/integer?`), strings;\n   602\t       - **Unambiguous keywords (`kind/keyword?`) and symbols (`kind/symbol?`):** letting `ns = (kind/namespace k)` and `nm = (kind/name k)`, `admit-key!` refuses with `{:clj.py/error :unsupported-key :key k}` whenever `ns` is empty (`\"\"`), `ns` contains `\"/\"` (`(not (nil? (data/str-index-of ns \"/\")))`), `nm` contains `\"/\"` (refusing `(keyword nil \"a/b\")` / `(symbol nil \"a/b\")` cleanly on EVERY host!), or `nm` begins with `\":\"` (`(if (> (data/str-length nm) 0) (= (data/substring nm 0 1) \":\") false)`). Because `(kind, ns, nm) -> joined-name` is strictly injective on admitted identifiers, CLJS joined-name map/set collapse (`dao.jing.cbor.md:266`) cannot happen;\n   603\t       - Persistent vectors, persistent maps (both keys and values checked recursively), and persistent sets recursively containing **only** admitted values.\n   604\t     - **Refused keys / set elements at ANY nesting depth:** any `data/float64?` value (`0.0`, `-0.0`, `1.0`, `NaN`, `±Inf`, or nested `[[-0.0]]`, `{\"a\" 1.0}`), ambiguous identifiers (`(keyword nil \"a/b\")`, `(symbol nil \"a/b\")`, `[(keyword nil \"a/b\")]`), lists/seqs (`seq?`, preventing list-vs-vector collisions), host closures/continuations, and `:cell-ref` handles — raising guest error `{:clj.py/error :unsupported-key :key k}` (`ex-info` in `clojure.core.impl`).\n   605\t     - Arbitrary floats (`-0.0`, `1.0`, `NaN`, `±Inf`), arbitrary identifiers (`(keyword nil \"a/b\")`), lists, and callables remain **fully supported as scalar values, map values, and vector/list elements**!\n   606\t   - **Recursive portable equality (`clj.py/eq`, `clj.py/ne` and `clojure.core.impl/impl-not=`):** Never delegates floats, float-bearing collections, or identifiers (keywords/symbols) to host `=`, because CLJS `Float64.-equiv` (`src/cljc/dao/host/number.cljc:98–101`) equates `NaN` with `NaN` and distinguishes `-0.0` from `0.0`, and CLJS identifier `=` equates `(keyword nil \"a/b\")` with `(keyword \"a\" \"b\")` (`dao.jing.cbor.md:266`):\n   607\t     - `:int` × `:int`: `(= (integer/compare a b) 0)`.\n   608\t     - `:float` × `:float`: leaf unwrap → `false` if either is NaN, else `(= ax bx)` (`+0.0 == -0.0` is `true`, `NaN == NaN` is `false` on all 4 hosts).\n   609\t     - `:int` × `:float` (or vice versa): **`false`** (`1 != 1.0`).\n   610\t     - Identifiers (`kind/keyword?`, `kind/symbol?`): compared strictly by kind + nullable namespace (`cmp-opt-str == 0`) + name (`(data/str-compare (kind/name a) (kind/name b)) == 0`), so `(keyword nil \"a/b\") == (keyword \"a\" \"b\")` is **`false`** on all 4 hosts including CLJS/Node.\n   611\t     - Vectors / sequential collections (`data/vector?`, `clojure.core.impl/impl-sequential?`): equal count + pairwise recursive `eq`.\n   612\t     - Maps (`data/map?`, excluding authenticated `:cell-ref` handles): equal count + every admitted key `k` present in both with values recursively equal via `eq` — so `{\"a\": -0.0} == {\"a\": 0.0}` is `true` and `{\"a\": NaN} == {\"a\": NaN}` is `false` on all 4 hosts.\n   613\t     - Sets (`kind/set?`): equal count + exact admitted membership across all elements.\n   614\t     - Other scalars (`nil`, booleans, strings, authenticated `:cell-ref` handles): host `=`.\n   615\t\n   616\t### 7.3 Python lowering Hook ABI & `clj.py` adapters\n   617\t\n   618\tRather than pretending `clj/*` shares identical signatures with `py/*`, the frontend keeps its fixed **Python Lowering Hook ABI** (`yang.python.antlr.contract`) and `clj.py` implements every hook with compatible arity and semantics:\n   619\t\n   620\t| Hook key | Frontend ABI signature | `clj.py` implementation |\n   621\t|---|---|---|\n   622\t| `:env/local-get` | `[cell name]` | Reads `(cell/get cell)`; raises guest unbound error if `:clj/unbound` (supporting parameter init, local reassignment, and `nonlocal` via shared lexical cells when `:mutation/locals :cell`). |\n   623\t| `:env/global-get` | `[globals-cell name]` | Reads `g = (cell/get globals-cell)`. Checks `(data/contains? (get g :vars) name)` first (returning module-level `def`/`global` bindings); on miss invokes the **unit-owned** `((get g :ambient) name)` resolver; if `:clj/unbound`, raises guest `NameError`-equivalent map built with evaluated `(assoc (assoc {} :clj.py/error :name-error) :name name)`. Two descriptors sharing the exact same `clj.py` address resolve completely independent alias tables inside the same task! |\n   624\t| `:env/global-set` | `[globals-cell name value]` | Writes `g = (cell/get globals-cell)` as `(cell/set! globals-cell (assoc g :vars (assoc (get g :vars) name value)))` (preserving `:ambient`) and returns `value`. |\n   625\t| `:fn/make` | `[fname spec defaults kwdefaults code]` | Accepts the exact 5 arguments from `yang.python.antlr.lower/function-value:1870` (lowering already refused defaults/kwonly/kwstar/kwargs when disabled); delegates directly to trusted Layer-2b **`clj/make-callable`** (`§7.4`) allocating a two-step authenticated task-heap cell. |\n   626\t| `:fn/call` | `[callee args]` | Delegates directly to trusted Layer-2b **`clj/invoke-callable`** (`§7.4`), which checks `clj/admitted-callable?` first and routes to `yang.call/invoke` with the condition-unwrapping / provenance-retaining raise exit. Zero provenance doors inside `clj.py`. |\n   627\t| `:ctrl/try` | `[body handler orelse]` | **3-arg signature** calling `yrt.escape/try-orelse` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` (sharing Clojure's exception domain by design), preserving Python `try` / `except` / `else`. |\n   628\t| `:ctrl/try-finally` | `[body fin]` | Calls `yrt.escape/try-finally` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` with `normal-arg = nil`. |\n   629\t| `:ctrl/raise` | `[e]` | Calls `clj/raise` (delegating to `yrt.escape/raise` on `(clj/rt-ctx)`). |\n   630\t| `:ctrl/call-ec` | `[f]` | Calls `yrt.escape/call-ec` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` with `normal-arg = nil`. |\n   631\t| `:ctrl/for-each` | `[iterable step-fn]` | Invokes collision-free implementation entries **`clojure.core.impl/impl-seq`**, **`impl-first`**, and **`impl-rest`** directly (zero collision with 0-arg public `clojure.core` export accessors!), iterates deterministic canonical `[k v]` pairs for maps and canonical elements for sets, raises guest error on non-collection iterables, and invokes `step-fn` per element (supports `break`/`continue` via `call-ec` and eager comprehensions). |\n   632\t| `:comp/list-new`, `:comp/set-new`, `:comp/dict-new` | `[init-vec]`, `[]`, `[]` | Allocates a temporary local accumulator cell holding persistent `[]`, `#{}`, or `{}` (`cell/new []`, `cell/new #{}`, `cell/new {}`). |\n   633\t| `:comp/list-append`, `:comp/set-add`, `:comp/dict-set` | `[acc val]`, `[acc val]`, `[acc k v]` | Reads `(cell/get acc)`, validates set elements / dict keys via `admit-key!`, updates via `(cell/set! acc (conj cur val))` / `(assoc cur k v)`, and returns `:py/None` (in `clj.py`, `nil`). |\n   634\t| `:comp/finish` | `[acc]` *(optional)* | Returns `(cell/get acc)` (the immutable persistent vector/set/map). Omitted (`nil`) in `:yang.python/py-v1` so mutable-accumulator Python lowering keeps zero overhead. |\n   635\t| `:unit/run-main` | `[body-fn ambient-resolver]` | Calls idempotent `(clj/init!)`, `(clojure.core/init!)`, and `(clj.py/init!)` (where `clj.py` exports idempotent 0-arg `init!`, 1-arg `export` via `clj/prim-get`, and 0-arg cell-accessor `ex-info`, satisfying `§6.4`'s `:cell-accessor` contract); allocates a **fresh per-unit `globals` cell** `(cell/new (assoc (assoc {} :vars {}) :ambient ambient-resolver))` and `globals-fn`; invokes `(body-fn globals globals-fn)` inside a top-level handler on `(clj/rt-ctx)`; returns the value **verbatim without stripping `[:yin.k/ok ...]`** so ordinary Python data shaped like `[:yin.k/ok 42]` passes through uncorrupted. |\n   636\t\n   637\t*(Lowerings with `:mutation/locals :single-assignment` remain a separate, stricter profile variant that omits local variable cells and refuses assignment/reassignment to locals, loops with mutated accumulators, and `nonlocal`.)*\n   638\t\n   639\t### 7.4 Unified trusted `clj` callable bridge, cross-unit admission, and §8.10.7 validation\n   640\t\n   641\tBecause `yang.call/eligible?` (`src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc:29–48`) only dereferences authenticated cell-refs and leaves ordinary maps intact, structural eligibility alone does **not** stop source-constructed maps carrying `:yang.call/entry` from masquerading as callables when source maps are first-class data. Under the Owner Clean-Slate Directive (no legacy runtime retention needed), all Clojure-family §8.10.7 callable/provenance bridging is unified directly into **trusted Layer-2b `clj`** (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc`, requiring `yang.call` and `yrt.escape`) — eliminating both any separate `clj.bridge` module AND `yang.clojure`'s legacy `dsg__call_token` / inline provenance code in P3!\n   642\t\n   643\t- `clj` owns the private provenance doors (`cell/dsg__new-provenance`, `cell/dsg__provenance`) inside **both** its linked (`module-uast`) and bundled (`uast`) emitters (preserving §5.2 Bundled vs. Linked Parity Law!), never exporting them and keeping them strictly out of `yrt.*`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core.impl`, and `clojure.core`.\n   644\t- `clj` also exports collision-free primitive helpers **`clj/prim-get`** (`(fn [m k] (get m k))`) and **`clj/prim-assoc`** (`(fn [m k v] (assoc m k v))`) — safe inside `clj` because `clj` has zero stripped exports named `get` or `assoc` in its module store (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:62–175`).\n   645\t\n   646\t`clj` enforces the full §8.10 + §8.10.7 contract:\n   647\t\n   648\t1. **Source-level callable admission (`clj/admitted-callable?`):**\n   649\t   - Called by `clj/invoke-callable`, `clj.py/callable?`, `clojure.core.impl/impl-fn?`, and `clojure.core.impl`'s dynamic higher-order caller **before** invoking `yang.call/invoke`. Written strictly in prelude special-form notation (`src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc:82` — nested `if`, zero `and` form!):\n   650\t     ```clojure\n   651\t     (if (data/map? x)\n   652\t       (if (= (get x :type) :cell-ref)\n   653\t         (if (cell/authentic? x)\n   654\t           (if (data/callable? (yang.call/entry x))\n   655\t             (yang.call/eligible? x)\n   656\t             false)\n   657\t           false)\n   658\t         false)\n   659\t       false)\n   660\t     ```\n   661\t   - Any plain source map (including `{:yang.call/entry ...}`), unauthenticated `{:type :cell-ref ...}` map, or raw host primitive/continuation fails `admitted-callable?` cleanly; `invoke-callable` mints a retained `:yang.call/not-callable` protocol condition via private `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and raises it via `(clj/raise ...)`, never calling `yang.call/invoke` on forged source data.\n   662\t   - Preserves zero-wrapper function identity (`=`) across all cell-backed frontends (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core`).\n   663\t2. **Two-step cell-backed callable constructor (`clj/make-callable`):**\n   664\t   - Given metadata map `meta` and binder/executor thunk `bind-and-run`, allocates the owner cell **first**, installs `entry` closing over that initialized `owner` binding via `cell/set!`, and returns `owner` (mirroring the working two-step pattern at `src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:944–960`):\n   665\t     ```clojure\n   666\t     (let [owner (cell/new meta)\n   667\t           entry (fn [invocation] ...)] ;; closes over `owner` & enforces Step 3\n   668\t       (do (cell/set! owner (assoc meta :yang.call/entry entry))\n   669\t           owner))\n   670\t     ```\n   671\t3. **Full 4-step invocation-record validation & §8.10.7 entry boundary (with evaluated `assoc` condition evidence):**\n   672\t   - **Step A — Establish usable raise exit first:** verify `(data/map? invocation)` and `(data/callable? (get invocation :yang.call/raise))`. If missing or non-callable, fail operationally right away (never invoke an invalid exit or convert wiring corruption into a guest catchable error).\n   673\t   - **Step B — Validate protocol record & owner identity (outside `try-value`):** check `(yang.call/valid-invocation? invocation)` AND `(= (get invocation :yang.call/callee) owner)`. Because `yang.core.uast/sexp->uast` emits map literals unevaluated (`src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc:82`), build the condition evidence via **evaluated `assoc` calls** before transferring:\n   674\t     ```clojure\n   675\t     (yang.call/transfer\n   676\t       raise-exit\n   677\t       (yang.call/condition :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n   678\t                            (assoc {} :yang.call/callee owner)))\n   679\t     ```\n   680\t   - **Step C — Reject unsupported binding extensions (outside `try-value`):** if `(data/contains? invocation :yang.call/binding-profile)`, build evidence with **evaluated `assoc` calls** and transfer:\n   681\t     ```clojure\n   682\t     (yang.call/transfer\n   683\t       raise-exit\n   684\t       (yang.call/condition\n   685\t         :yang.call/unsupported-binding\n   686\t         (assoc (assoc {} :yang.call/callee owner)\n   687\t                :yang.call/binding-profile (get invocation :yang.call/binding-profile))))\n   688\t     ```\n   689\t   - **Step D — Value-returning boundary (`yrt.escape/try-value` — NOT `try-orelse`!) around binding + body:**\n   690\t     - Installs the exception handler on `(clj/rt-ctx)` **before** argument binding so ordinary named-arg / positional-arity errors share the same boundary: inside `try-value`, `(bind-and-run positional named)` checks `:yang.call/named` and positional/varargs arity against `:spec` (raising local guest binding exceptions via `clj/raise` so they cross under **`:yang.call/thrown`**) and evaluates the body.\n   691\t     - On normal completion, `yrt.escape/try-value` restores `(clj/rt-ctx)` and returns the body's value verbatim (`20` in §7.6).\n   692\t     - On escape with `e`, the handler inspects private `(cell/dsg__provenance e)`: if non-nil (an authentic retained protocol condition from a deeper cross-language boundary), forwards that retained condition **directly** to `raise-exit` without double-wrapping; otherwise wraps `e` (including condition-shaped user maps!) via `(yang.call/thrown e)` and transfers it to `raise-exit`.\n   693\t4. **Call-site boundary (`clj/invoke-callable`):**\n   694\t   - Validates `(clj/admitted-callable? callee)`; if false, mints private retained `:yang.call/not-callable` via `cell/dsg__new-provenance` (with evaluated `(assoc {} :yang.call/callee callee)` evidence) and raises on `(clj/rt-ctx)`.\n   695\t   - Otherwise calls `yang.call/invoke` with a dedicated `raise-exit` closure:\n   696\t     - If `(= (get condition :yang.call/reason) :yang.call/thrown)`, calls `(clj/raise (get condition :yang.call/value))` (unwrapping user-thrown values).\n   697\t     - Otherwise retains the protocol condition inside a private provenance carrier `(clj/raise (cell/dsg__new-provenance condition condition))`, preserving full condition fidelity across `A → B → A` unwinds and `finally` blocks, as well as nested `clj → clj.py → clj` unwinding on `(clj/rt-ctx)`.\n   698\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
