{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc | sed -n '226,294p' && rg -n ':yin.k/arities|host-export-profile' src/cljc/yang src/cljc/yin/vm/{module,linker}.cljc | head -45\"","aggregated_output":"   226\t\n   227\t(defn register-host-module\n   228\t  \"Return registry with host module `module-name` installed from `fns`\n   229\t   under `profiles`.\n   230\t\n   231\t   module-name is a dotted symbol; fns maps each export symbol to the host\n   232\t   value it publishes; profiles maps each export symbol to its UCF 7.5.2\n   233\t   profile record in the shape of `yin.vm/primitive-profiles`. Every\n   234\t   binding must carry a profile, and the profile's class must be `:pure`,\n   235\t   or `:effectful` with a declared, non-empty `:yin.k/effects` set, with\n   236\t   `:yin.k/host-state` `:none`. An `:effectful` export returns an\n   237\t   effect minted by `make-effect` for the engine to interpret and\n   238\t   performs no IO itself; `stream/make` is exactly such a constructor.\n   239\t   Each export's declared effect set is also entered in the registry's\n   240\t   identity-keyed `:callable-effects`, which the engine checks an\n   241\t   effect's kind against (D4).\n   242\t\n   243\t   The module is entered as an already-linked manifest with\n   244\t   `:yin.module/tree` absent, `:yin.module/derivations {}`, and its\n   245\t   exports listed under `:yin.module/primitives` by profile address; the\n   246\t   exports themselves are its `:slice`, and its `:address` and\n   247\t   `:derivation` are nil because no content was fetched or derived: the\n   248\t   host is the boundary.\"\n   249\t  [registry module-name fns profiles]\n   250\t  (doseq [sym (sort-by str (keys fns))]\n   251\t    (check-binding! module-name sym (get profiles sym)))\n   252\t  (-> (or registry (empty-registry))\n   253\t      (update :callable-effects\n   254\t              (partial merge-with into)\n   255\t              (vm/callable-effects fns profiles))\n   256\t      (assoc-in (into [:modules] (symbol->path module-name))\n   257\t                {:manifest {:yin.module/name module-name,\n   258\t                            :yin.module/derivations {},\n   259\t                            :yin.module/primitives\n   260\t                            (into {} (map (fn [[sym _f]]\n   261\t                                            [sym (:yin.k/profile\n   262\t                                                   (get profiles sym))]))\n   263\t                                  fns)},\n   264\t                 :address nil,\n   265\t                 :derivation nil,\n   266\t                 :slice fns,\n   267\t                 :stores {}})))\n   268\t\n   269\t\n   270\t(defn host-export-profile\n   271\t  \"The profile address host module `ns` publishes for export `name`, when\n   272\t   `qualified-sym` is `ns/name` and `registry` holds `ns` as a\n   273\t   host-registered entry (`register-host-module`'s shape, `:address`\n   274\t   nil); else nil. A linked entry never answers: the\n   275\t   `:yin.module/primitives` of a fetched manifest are the primitives that\n   276\t   module assumes, not exports it provides.\"\n   277\t  [registry qualified-sym]\n   278\t  (when (and (symbol? qualified-sym) (some? (namespace qualified-sym)))\n   279\t    (let [entry (module-entry (:modules registry)\n   280\t                              (symbol (namespace qualified-sym)))]\n   281\t      (when (and (some? entry) (nil? (:address entry)))\n   282\t        (get-in entry [:manifest :yin.module/primitives\n   283\t                       (symbol (name qualified-sym))])))))\n   284\t\n   285\t\n   286\t;; =============================================================================\n   287\t;; Effect descriptors\n   288\t;; =============================================================================\n   289\t\n   290\t;; An effect is the host type `yin.vm.effect/Effect` (D4): `effect?` is a\n   291\t;; type test, and a map is data whatever keys it carries. `make-effect` is\n   292\t;; the trusted constructor for host code; it is never a guest primitive or\n   293\t;; module export.\n   294\t\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:1003:   (`module/host-export-profile`) -- a module obligation only by a linked\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:1017:                         (= profile (module/host-export-profile\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:189:  [:yin.k/profile :yin.k/class :yin.k/arities :yin.k/effects\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:270:(defn host-export-profile\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:249:          (into {} (map (fn [op] [op (:yin.k/arities (get data/data-profiles op))]))\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1343:   of its `:yin.k/arities` profile, extended to `adapter-variadic-cap` when\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2167:   its published profile, whose `:yin.k/arities` give an adapter its admitted\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2199:                                                                       (:yin.k/arities profile)\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/prelude_admission.cljc:20:    (when-let [address (module/host-export-profile registry n)]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
