{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '1356,1415p' && rg -n '(:yin.module/requires|missing-requirement|dependency-conflict|dependency.*linked|linked.*dependency)' src/cljc/yin/vm/{engine,kernel,module,linker}.cljc | tail -100\"","aggregated_output":"  1356\t  inside wait restoration.\n  1357\t- **The requiring task waits on the install, not on the linker.** Once\n  1358\t  the child starts, the parent's entry becomes\n  1359\t  `{:reason :install :name 'foo}`, and any other task that requires\n  1360\t  `'foo` meanwhile joins `:waiters`. No task is restored until the\n  1361\t  install reaches `linked` or `refused`.\n  1362\t- **`running` may park.** A module body that reads a stream, calls FFI,\n  1363\t  or requires another module parks the child exactly as any task parks;\n  1364\t  a transitive require emits its own link request under its own id\n  1365\t  (section 7.4). The parent is parked on `:install` and is unaffected;\n  1366\t  the scheduler keeps stepping every other task. There is nothing to\n  1367\t  deadlock on except a cycle, which section 7.4 refuses.\n  1368\t- **`validated` requires halt plus exports.** The child must reach halt\n  1369\t  (not error, not an abandoned park), and every name under\n  1370\t  `:yin.module/exports` must be a key of the child's store. A missing\n  1371\t  export is `:export-missing`; an error is the error. Nothing from a\n  1372\t  refused child's store is published.\n  1373\t- **`linked` lifts the exports; each receiver relocates them.** A\n  1374\t  child's store holds closures whose code coordinates are the child's:\n  1375\t  a stack or register closure carries a body pc into the child's held\n  1376\t  segment and no image identity; a semantic closure carries a local\n  1377\t  segment id minted by the child's loader. Published as they are, those\n  1378\t  coordinates are meaningless in the parent, so bindings cross the\n  1379\t  child-to-parent boundary the way a continuation crosses any boundary:\n  1380\t  by lift and lower. The `linked` transition is four acts: acts 1\n  1381\t  and 2 run once, at `validated`; acts 3 and 4 run once per\n  1382\t  receiving task -- the parent at `linked`, and each waiter or later\n  1383\t  requirer at its own restore.\n  1384\t  Before act 1, every present `:yin.module/requires` dependency must have\n  1385\t  the halted child's linked entry at its pinned manifest address.\n  1386\t  Present-and-unequal refuses `:dependency-pin-mismatch` with `:module`,\n  1387\t  `:name`, `:pinned`, and `:linked`, choosing the first mismatch by name\n  1388\t  string order. Absence is permitted at install for deferred dependencies.\n  1389\t  At each receive (child inheritance and parent acts 3 and 4), the registry\n  1390\t  pin invariant checks both existing manifests' pins for the incoming name\n  1391\t  and the incoming manifest's pins for held names, before any attachment or\n  1392\t  lowering. Thus a deferred name can only bind at its pinned address.\n  1393\t  Nothing is published on refusal; every waiter receives the refusal.\n  1394\t  1. *The child's export slice is lifted* to UCF's portable encoding\n  1395\t     (section 7.5.1, amended below): each closure becomes a\n  1396\t     `:yin.k/closure` marker naming its **origin image** and its entry\n  1397\t     relative to that image, with its captured values encoded\n  1398\t     recursively; every other value encodes by the same grammar. The\n  1399\t     origin is not assumed to be the module's own image: a closure the\n  1400\t     child obtained from a dependency and re-exported originates in\n  1401\t     that dependency's image, and the lift records whichever image the\n  1402\t     closure's coordinates fall in. The lift is refused as\n  1403\t     `:yin.k/non-portable` for the same leaves UCF refuses (a host\n  1404\t     object, an in-memory handle), and a refused lift refuses the\n  1405\t     install: an export that cannot cross a boundary is not an export.\n  1406\t  2. *The origin set is checked.* The lifted slice's\n  1407\t     `:yin.k/requires :yin.k/segments` enumerates every origin image it\n  1408\t     names, transitively through captured values. Each must be an image\n  1409\t     this scheduler verified: the module's own, or one delivered for an\n  1410\t     install in this scheduler's history (held under `:installs` or the\n  1411\t     registry by identity). An origin identity the scheduler never\n  1412\t     verified is `:foreign-image`, and the install is refused; a\n  1413\t     verified image is never re-fetched for this step.\n  1414\t  3. *The receiving task attaches every origin image its kernel does\n  1415\t     not yet hold*, non-destructively. The ordinary loaders\nrg: src/cljc/yin/vm/kernel.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:744:    :yin.module/exports :yin.module/requires :yin.module/primitives\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:773:                         (concat (keys (:yin.module/requires manifest))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:824:          (when-not (name-map? manifest :yin.module/requires address?)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:825:            (shape :yin.module/requires))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:2069:   carrying the profile address; a name under `:yin.module/requires` --\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:2076:        requires (:yin.module/requires manifest)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:119:   would disagree with a linked manifest's dependency pin. Missing\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:125:                         (let [requires (:yin.module/requires (:manifest e))]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:136:                       (:yin.module/requires (:manifest entry)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1227:        requires (set (keys (:yin.module/requires manifest)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1395:              (sort-by (comp str key) (:yin.module/requires manifest)))]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1466:   dependency -- refuses it too, at phase `:linked`, from the state the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"The revised design resolves the original linker name collision and callable-owner construction. I’m checking two remaining integration points against the live code: how a cold task loads dependencies, and how the shared entry hook carries PHP’s request and output streams."}}
