{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '297,345p;431,447p;480,497p;507,524p;598,605p;620,627p;735,747p;801,831p'\"","aggregated_output":"   297\t   - Admission takes `(profile artifact-store registry)`, where `artifact-store` supplies an **immutable, verified content-addressed map** of published manifests (`manifest-addr -> verified-manifest`) AND their referenced canonical module trees (`tree-addr -> verified-uast`) — never assuming a graph from bare `[sym addr]` pairs!\n   298\t   - Separately checks **direct root pins** and the **transitive closure**:\n   299\t     - Every `[sym addr]` in `:yang.prelude/components` and `:yang.prelude/root-address` resolves in `artifact-store`, and the root manifest's direct `:requires` map matches `:yang.prelude/components` (pinning direct edges without requiring transitive-only dependencies such as `clj` via `clojure.core` to be duplicated at the root).\n   300\t     - Recursively walks every `:requires` edge starting from `:yang.prelude/root-address` across `artifact-store`, verifying that every transitively reachable manifest address and `:yin.module/tree` address resolves, that the full transitive `:requires` DAG is finite and acyclic, and that no two distinct addresses bind the same linker module symbol anywhere in the closure.\n   301\t2. **Export collision rule (qualified vs. projected):**\n   302\t   - Distinct Layer-2a/2b/2c modules **may** share identical bare local export names (for instance, `yrt.float/abs` and `py/abs` coexist safely across qualified module borders).\n   303\t   - Collisions **are refused** whenever two components bind the same linker module symbol, when a local `module-definitions` key collides after namespace stripping, or when two source-facing `:ambient-projections` claim the same target identifier (`§6.3`).\n   304\t3. **Provenance-door security exclusion (direct declarations, not transitive footprint):**\n   305\t   - Because `yin.vm.linker.publish/footprint` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:81`) unions dependency effects transitively into `:yin.module/footprint`, a consumer like `clojure.core` requiring trusted `clj` legitimately carries `:cell/new-provenance` / `:cell/provenance` in its transitive `:yin.module/footprint`.\n   306\t   - Therefore, validation enforces the provenance-door exclusion against each non-trusted module's (`yrt.*`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core.impl`, `clojure.core`) **direct** `:yin.module/primitives` (refusing `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and `cell/dsg__provenance`) and **direct** `:yin.module/exports` (refusing any `dsg__*` export on **every** module including trusted Layer-2b runtimes), while governing transitive effects through `:yang.prelude/max-effects` below.\n   307\t4. **Effect-ceiling verification (`:yang.prelude/max-effects`):**\n   308\t   - Rather than duplicating the manifest's derived effect set (honoring \"Derive, don't persist\"), `:yang.prelude/max-effects` is strictly optional. When present, admission checks `(clojure.set/subset? derived-transitive-effects max-effects)` using the verified `:yin.module/footprint :effects` union and refuses if any transitive module (including any `:module/require` from `:trailing-requires`) or host declaration exceeds the ceiling.\n   309\t5. **Host-module and limit admission (`admit-profile`):**\n   310\t   - Because `yin.vm.module/register-host-module` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:249`) stores exports and profiles without retaining raw limit declarations (`yin.vm.integer` does not export `integer/max-bits`, and `yang.python.antlr.prelude/register-integer-module:4163` validates an explicit `limits` map before registration), **`admit-profile` takes `(profile artifact-store registry host-limits)`**.\n   311\t   - Verifies that `registry` supplies every required host export (`prelude-admission/admit`) AND verifies every declared floor in `:yang.prelude/host-modules` (`:min-bits`, `:min-digits`, `:min-max-items`) against the trusted composition `host-limits` map (failing closed if `host-limits` is absent or below the required floor, and cross-checking `integer/max-digits` / `data/max-items` against `host-limits` when present).\n   312\t6. **Dual-emitter standardization & Parity Law:**\n   313\t   - **Standardized linked emission (`P0` clean-slate normalization):** derives `:requires` and `:skip?` directly from `:yang.prelude/components`; emits trailing `require` forms **only** from explicit `:trailing-requires` (`[]` for standardized base preludes `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj`/`yang.call`, `['py]`/`['js]` only for safepoint overlays `py.sp`/`js.sp`); preserves `:rt-namespaces`; runs optional local unshadowing (`php`); and enables `:finalize-c1? true` uniformly across all emitted module trees (standardizing `py`, `php`, and `py.sp` onto the same C1 contract as `js`, `clj`, `js.sp`, and `yang.call`).\n   314\t   - **Bundled emission (`compose-bundled`):** preserves operand ordering, `init!` placement, tail-marking, `:mode` (`:linear` vs `:balanced`), and Clojure's bundled preamble/wrappers until P3 migrates Clojure onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core`.\n   315\t   - **Bundled vs. Linked Parity Law:** Any program compiled under a composed prelude MUST produce identical outcomes in bundled and linked modes across the semantic, stack, and register VMs (and the AST walker once L-b lands).\n   316\t\n   317\t---\n   318\t\n   319\t## 6. Preludes as swappable libraries: the semantics descriptor contract\n   320\t\n   321\tMaking Layer-2a components reusable solves code duplication; making **Layer-2b/2c preludes swappable libraries** solves syntax-to-runtime coupling. A frontend like `yang.python` can then treat its runtime prelude as a pluggable library (`:yang.semantics/descriptor`).\n   322\t\n   323\t### 6.1 Level 1 vs. Level 2 library composition\n   324\t\n   325\t- **Level 1 — Ambient Library Projection:** Keep the frontend's native semantics (`py`, `js`, `php`) and link an external module (such as `clojure.core`) into its ambient lookup scope via `yang.call`.\n   326\t- **Level 2 — Pluggable Semantics Library:** Replace the frontend's lowering contract itself with a compatible prelude library (e.g., compiling Python syntax against `clojure.core` + `clj` directly onto persistent Yin data structures with zero value wrapping or marshalling).\n   327\t\n   328\tLevel 2 strictly subsumes Level 1: a semantics descriptor defines **both** what lowering emits for syntax constructs (`:yang.semantics/hooks` + `:yang.semantics/literals`) and which ambient modules/identifiers enter source scope (`:yang.semantics/ambient-modules` + `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`).\n   329\t\n   330\t### 6.2 Core vs. Frontend ownership boundary\n   331\t\n   332\tTo preserve `yang.antlr.md` §3 (\"Yang core contains no enumeration of supported languages\"):\n   333\t- **`yang.core.semantics` (language-agnostic)** owns ONLY:\n   334\t  1. Generic schema validation for `:yang.semantics/descriptor`.\n   335\t  2. Pure, closed literal-strategy emission (`:raw`, `:float64-raw`, `:tagged-map`, `:raw-or-call`).\n   336\t  3. Generic capability lookup, hook-hygiene validation (every hook must be namespace-qualified), UAST-derived structural export/arity/role verification against the descriptor's **selected, address-verified closure** across **every** executable descriptor field (hooks, executable literal strategies such as `:literals.*.overflow-op`, and ambient projections), and reserved-door projection checks.\n   337\t- **Each frontend package (e.g. `yang.python.antlr.contract`)** owns:\n   338\t  1. Its **fixed Hook ABI table** (`{hook-key {:arity n :required-by [...]}}`) specifying exact parameter conventions and structural lowering shapes for that frontend's grammar.\n   339\t  2. Structural AST lowering rules (e.g., how Python functions, loops, comprehensions, module packets, and `try`/`except`/`else`/`finally` marshal operands to those hooks).\n   340\t\n   341\t`yang.core.semantics` validates a descriptor **against the frontend-supplied contract table** — core never hardcodes Python, JS, or PHP syntax constructs.\n   342\t\n   343\t### 6.3 Portable `:yang.semantics/descriptor` schema\n   344\t\n   345\tA semantics descriptor contains **only portable data** (satisfies `yang.frontend/non-portable-path`):\n   431\t  :fn/make          'clj.py/make-fn\n   432\t  :fn/call          'clj.py/call\n   433\t  ;; Control flow & unit entry (unit/run-main always takes `[body-fn ambient-resolver]`)\n   434\t  :ctrl/for-each    'clj.py/for-each\n   435\t  :ctrl/try         'clj.py/try\n   436\t  :ctrl/try-finally 'clj.py/try-finally\n   437\t  :ctrl/raise       'clj.py/raise\n   438\t  :ctrl/call-ec     'clj.py/call-ec\n   439\t  :unit/run-main    'clj.py/run-main}\n   440\t\n   441\t ;; Each entry defaults to :kind :cell-accessor (emitted per unit into `ambient-resolver` as\n   442\t ;; `(m/e)`, returning the module's stable task-local authenticated callable cell); optional\n   443\t ;; :kind :value references a non-lambda immutable export directly.\n   444\t :yang.semantics/ambient-projections\n   445\t {\"identity\"  {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'identity,  :kind :cell-accessor}\n   446\t  \"inc\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'inc,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n   447\t  \"dec\"       {:module 'clojure.core, :export 'dec,       :kind :cell-accessor}\n   480\t2. **Scope-aware precedence for `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`:**\n   481\t   - Free source identifiers resolve in strict order:\n   482\t     1. **Lexical scope** (`:local`, `:cell`, `:nonlocal` parameter or local variable, including a local named `map` or `conj`),\n   483\t     2. **Per-module globals** (`:vars` map inside the unit's `globals-cell` via `:env/global-get`, allowing module-level `def` or `global` assignment to shadow an ambient binding cleanly),\n   484\t     3. **Unit-bound ambient resolver** (`:ambient` function stored inside that unit's own `globals-cell`, synthesized purely at lowering time from the descriptor's `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` and passed via `:unit/run-main`), failing with a guest `NameError` if absent.\n   485\t   - Defining or binding a parameter named `conj` or `is_empty` shadows only that source lookup and **never** alters compiler-generated calls to `clj.py/vconj`, `clj.py/add`, etc.\n   486\t3. **UAST-derived structural export & reserved-door authority validation against the selected closure (`validate-descriptor`):**\n   487\t   - Takes `(descriptor frontend-contract artifact-store registry)`:\n   488\t     - Computes the descriptor's **selected, address-verified closure**: every `[module address]` in `:yang.semantics/ambient-modules` must resolve in `artifact-store` (both its verified manifest AND its `:yin.module/tree` canonical UAST) along with its full transitive `:requires` DAG (with unique module-symbol bindings).\n   489\t     - Inspects **every executable reference anywhere in the descriptor**: every active hook in `:yang.semantics/hooks` (including non-nil optional hooks such as `:comp/finish`), every executable literal-strategy field (such as `:yang.semantics/literals.*.overflow-op`), and every `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` target (`{:module m :export e :kind k}`).\n   490\t     - Because Schema-1 `:yin.module/exports` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:375`) records only a set of export names without arity or role metadata, `validate-descriptor` inspects the target manifest's verified `:yin.module/tree` UAST (`yang.core.prelude/wide-app` top-level `(yin/def (quote sym) expr)` definitions per `src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc:35–56`) directly inside `artifact-store`:\n   491\t       - **Hooks and executable `:literals.*` targets:** verifies the symbol is namespace-qualified, exists in `:yin.module/exports` of `m` in the **selected, address-verified closure** (or an authorized host module in `registry` required by that closure, checked against `:yin.k/arities`), and its verified UAST definition `expr` is a `:lambda` whose `(count (:params expr))` **equals** the exact arity required by `frontend-contract` (rejecting any module that exposes the right export name with the wrong arity or a non-lambda binding!).\n   492\t       - **Ambient projections (`:kind :cell-accessor`, the default):** checks unique alias names, verifies `e` exists in `:yin.module/exports` of `m`, verifies `e`'s UAST definition in `m`'s `:yin.module/tree` is a **0-arg `:lambda`** (`:params []`), AND verifies `m` exports `init!` (0-arg `:lambda`) and `export` (1-arg `:lambda`). (Behavioral properties — such as idempotence of `init!` and `export` returning an authenticated `yang.call` cell — are certified by conformance tests pinned to that exact module content address.)\n   493\t       - **Ambient projections (`:kind :value`):** verifies `e` exists in `:yin.module/exports` of `m` and its UAST definition in `:yin.module/tree` is a non-lambda value (`:literal`, or safe constructor form without free side effects).\n   494\t       - An export belonging to an unrelated manifest somewhere else in `artifact-store` outside the descriptor's selected closure is **rejected**.\n   495\t     - **Reserved-door ban:** Refuses any descriptor whose `:hooks`, executable `:literals.*` fields, or `:ambient-projections` references `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, `yang.safepoint/*`, or internal implementation modules `*.impl/*` (such as `clojure.core.impl/*`), or exposes any unprivileged raw primitive without projection. Registry availability never grants source-level authority.\n   496\t   - Any violation fails closed before reading CST packets with `:yang.semantics/invalid-descriptor`.\n   497\t4. **Fail-closed capability enforcement during lowering:**\n   507\t      :node <cst-node-id>}\n   508\t     ```\n   509\t5. **Default-profile & cross-frontend parameterization parity (`P2`):**\n   510\t   - `yang.python.antlr.lower` (along with TypeScript, PHP, and `yang.clojure` lowerings in **Slice P2**) reads literals, hooks (including `:unit/run-main` `[body-fn ambient-resolver]` and comprehension hooks with `:comp/finish nil` for `py-v1`), capabilities, and projections from `:yang.semantics/descriptor`.\n   511\t   - Under `:yang.python/py-v1`, this preserves **full CPython behavioral/oracle and 4-host execution parity** cleanly (regenerating any affected goldens cleanly when `:unit/run-main` adopts the uniform 2-arg ABI across frontends), while parameterizing `yang.clojure` enables **symmetric cross-frontend prelude swapping** (e.g., compiling `yang.clojure` syntax onto `py` in a future profile alongside Python onto `clojure.core` in P3).\n   512\t\n   513\t### 6.5 Frontend SPI and provenance integration (`yang.frontend`)\n   514\t\n   515\tNo `yang.frontend` schema change is required (`src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc`):\n   516\t- `:yang.frontend/id` continues to name the frontend syntax + lowering implementation (e.g., `:yang.python/antlr`), and each distinct configuration receives a distinct immutable `:yang.frontend/revision` (e.g., `\"py-v1\"` vs. `\"clojure-core-v1\"` — re-installing `[id revision]` with a different manifest returns `:yang.frontend/revision-conflict`).\n   517\t- `:yang.frontend/lowering-profile` pins the content address of the `:yang.semantics/descriptor` EDN artifact.\n   518\t- `:yang.frontend/runtime-profile` pins the content address of the resolved `:yang.prelude/profile` manifest.\n   519\t- Compilation provenance records `(cst-address, lowering-profile, runtime-profile, unit-address)` as data; note that distinct descriptors may legitimately yield identical UAST addresses on simple programs (many-to-one), so provenance retains the exact compilation tuple rather than inferring the descriptor from the UAST address alone.\n   520\t\n   521\t---\n   522\t\n   523\t## 7. Case study: `yang.python` with a `clojure.core` prelude (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`)\n   524\t\n   598\t   - **Why a uniform key/element gate is required (`yin/vm/data.cljc:34–36`, `dao.jing.cbor.md:173, 266`):** Host map/set hashing and Jing canonical CBOR encoding cannot recover distinct keys once collapsed by host collection construction (`1` vs `1.0`, `[[-0.0]]`, `NaN`, OR `(keyword nil \"a/b\")` vs. `(keyword \"a\" \"b\")` on CLJS), and host map/set lookup diverges across JVM (`1 != 1.0`) vs JS (`1 == 1.0` and joined keyword strings).\n   599\t   - **One uniform `v1` portable key/element admission gate (`admit-key!`):** Enforced across BOTH `clj.py` (`map-from`, `set-from`, `get-item`, `comp-set-add`, `comp-dict-set`) AND `clojure.core.impl` (`impl-assoc`, `impl-assoc-in`, `impl-update`, `impl-update-in`, `impl-get`, `impl-get-in`, `impl-contains?`, `impl-conj` on maps/sets, `impl-disj`, `impl-merge`, `impl-into` targeting maps/sets, `impl-union`, `impl-difference`, `impl-hash-map`, `impl-set`, `impl-get-coll`, `impl-assoc-coll`, `impl-conj-coll`):\n   600\t     - **Admitted keys / set elements (recursively):**\n   601\t       - `nil`, booleans, exact integers (`integer/integer?`), strings;\n   602\t       - **Unambiguous keywords (`kind/keyword?`) and symbols (`kind/symbol?`):** letting `ns = (kind/namespace k)` and `nm = (kind/name k)`, `admit-key!` refuses with `{:clj.py/error :unsupported-key :key k}` whenever `ns` is empty (`\"\"`), `ns` contains `\"/\"` (`(not (nil? (data/str-index-of ns \"/\")))`), `nm` contains `\"/\"` (refusing `(keyword nil \"a/b\")` / `(symbol nil \"a/b\")` cleanly on EVERY host!), or `nm` begins with `\":\"` (`(if (> (data/str-length nm) 0) (= (data/substring nm 0 1) \":\") false)`). Because `(kind, ns, nm) -> joined-name` is strictly injective on admitted identifiers, CLJS joined-name map/set collapse (`dao.jing.cbor.md:266`) cannot happen;\n   603\t       - Persistent vectors, persistent maps (both keys and values checked recursively), and persistent sets recursively containing **only** admitted values.\n   604\t     - **Refused keys / set elements at ANY nesting depth:** any `data/float64?` value (`0.0`, `-0.0`, `1.0`, `NaN`, `±Inf`, or nested `[[-0.0]]`, `{\"a\" 1.0}`), ambiguous identifiers (`(keyword nil \"a/b\")`, `(symbol nil \"a/b\")`, `[(keyword nil \"a/b\")]`), lists/seqs (`seq?`, preventing list-vs-vector collisions), host closures/continuations, and `:cell-ref` handles — raising guest error `{:clj.py/error :unsupported-key :key k}` (`ex-info` in `clojure.core.impl`).\n   605\t     - Arbitrary floats (`-0.0`, `1.0`, `NaN`, `±Inf`), arbitrary identifiers (`(keyword nil \"a/b\")`), lists, and callables remain **fully supported as scalar values, map values, and vector/list elements**!\n   620\t| Hook key | Frontend ABI signature | `clj.py` implementation |\n   621\t|---|---|---|\n   622\t| `:env/local-get` | `[cell name]` | Reads `(cell/get cell)`; raises guest unbound error if `:clj/unbound` (supporting parameter init, local reassignment, and `nonlocal` via shared lexical cells when `:mutation/locals :cell`). |\n   623\t| `:env/global-get` | `[globals-cell name]` | Reads `g = (cell/get globals-cell)`. Checks `(data/contains? (get g :vars) name)` first (returning module-level `def`/`global` bindings); on miss invokes the **unit-owned** `((get g :ambient) name)` resolver; if `:clj/unbound`, raises guest `NameError`-equivalent map built with evaluated `(assoc (assoc {} :clj.py/error :name-error) :name name)`. Two descriptors sharing the exact same `clj.py` address resolve completely independent alias tables inside the same task! |\n   624\t| `:env/global-set` | `[globals-cell name value]` | Writes `g = (cell/get globals-cell)` as `(cell/set! globals-cell (assoc g :vars (assoc (get g :vars) name value)))` (preserving `:ambient`) and returns `value`. |\n   625\t| `:fn/make` | `[fname spec defaults kwdefaults code]` | Accepts the exact 5 arguments from `yang.python.antlr.lower/function-value:1870` (lowering already refused defaults/kwonly/kwstar/kwargs when disabled); delegates directly to trusted Layer-2b **`clj/make-callable`** (`§7.4`) allocating a two-step authenticated task-heap cell. |\n   626\t| `:fn/call` | `[callee args]` | Delegates directly to trusted Layer-2b **`clj/invoke-callable`** (`§7.4`), which checks `clj/admitted-callable?` first and routes to `yang.call/invoke` with the condition-unwrapping / provenance-retaining raise exit. Zero provenance doors inside `clj.py`. |\n   627\t| `:ctrl/try` | `[body handler orelse]` | **3-arg signature** calling `yrt.escape/try-orelse` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` (sharing Clojure's exception domain by design), preserving Python `try` / `except` / `else`. |\n   735\t3. **Public cell-free facade `clojure.core` (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/core_module.cljc`):**\n   736\t   - Requires **`clj`** and **`clojure.core.impl`**. Exports ONLY cell-free pure functions at install time (`src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:915, 1055`):\n   737\t     1. Internal non-exported runtime placeholders `clojure.core.rt/state` and `clojure.core.rt/exports` start at `:clojure.core/uninit`.\n   738\t     2. **`clojure.core/init!` (`[]`):** Idempotent per-task initializer — checks `(= clojure.core.rt/state :clojure.core/uninit)` (safe because `=` is not exported by `clojure.core`), calls `(clj/init!)`, builds `{sym cell}` using **`clj/prim-assoc`** (NEVER bare `assoc`!) and `(clj/make-callable meta wrapper-for-impl-*)` for every public export (`identity`, `inc`, `dec`, `str`, `count`, `first`, `rest`, `second`, `cons`, `conj`, `assoc`, `assoc-in`, `get`, `get-in`, `update`, `update-in`, `map`, `filter`, `reduce`, `into`, `keys`, `vals`, `merge`, `empty?`, `nil?`, `map?`, `vector?`, `set?`, etc.), stores it via `(yin/def (quote clojure.core.rt/exports) (cell/new export-map))`, and flips `(yin/def (quote clojure.core.rt/state) :clojure.core/ready)`.\n   739\t     3. **`clojure.core/export` (`[sym]`):** Calls `(clojure.core/init!)` and returns **`(clj/prim-get (cell/get clojure.core.rt/exports) sym)`** — using qualified `clj/prim-get` so looking up `sym` NEVER recurses into `clojure.core`'s stripped `get` store entry! Two importers in one task receive the identical (`=`) cell; two tasks receive isolated cells.\n   740\t     4. **Public 0-arg cell-accessor exports:** For every public library function `<name>`, `clojure.core` exports `(fn [] (clojure.core/export (quote <name>)))`. Because zero `:cell-ref` values exist in `:slice`, `lift-slice` succeeds uniformly across all 4 hosts, `validate-descriptor` verifies the 0-arg `:lambda` shape directly in `clojure.core`'s verified UAST tree, and callers obtain the stable task-local cell by calling `(clojure.core/<name>)`.\n   741\t   - **Dynamic closure construction & internal call discipline:**\n   742\t     - Closures returned at runtime by `impl-comp` and `impl-partial` are constructed via **`clj/make-callable`** (preserving cross-unit authenticated cell identity `=`), static sibling calls inside `clojure.core.impl` invoke stripped `impl-*` lambdas directly, and all dynamic callbacks (`f` in `impl-map`, `impl-filter`, `impl-remove`, `impl-reduce`, `impl-update`, `impl-update-in`, `impl-comp`, `impl-partial`) go exclusively through **`clj/invoke-callable`**.\n   743\t4. **No implicit namespace dump & clean unification of `yang.clojure` in P3:**\n   744\t   - Adding `'clojure.core` to `:requires` exposes nothing to user code on its own; only explicit entries in `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` enter source scope.\n   745\t   - Under the Owner Clean-Slate Directive, **Slice P3 migrates `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core`** (retiring `yang.clojure`'s old inline `library-for` duplication, unit-local `dsg__call_token` admission, and inline provenance ops cleanly — zero dual stdlib!).\n   746\t\n   747\t### 7.6 Concrete lowering example\n   801\t| Slice | Scope & deliverables | Golden impact | Concrete acceptance gate |\n   802\t|---|---|---|---|\n   803\t| **P0 — Uniform composition plumbing & `defquoted` consolidation** | Consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.prelude`; implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` (with independent `:components`, explicit `:trailing-requires`, uniform `:finalize-c1? true`) / `:yang.prelude/profile`, `validate-profile` (direct `:yin.module/primitives`/`:exports` provenance ban vs. transitive `:yin.module/footprint` ceiling; verified `:yin.module/tree` closure), and `admit-profile` (explicit `host-limits`); standardize `py`, `js`, `php`, `clj`, `yang.call` base preludes (`:trailing-requires []`, `:finalize-c1? true`; safepoint overlays keep explicit `:trailing-requires ['py]` / `['js]`). | Regenerate `py`/`php`/`py.sp` cleanly | Direct-vs.-transitive `:requires` closure tests (including transitive-only deps), missing manifest/`:yin.module/tree` refusal, `host-limits` numeric-floor enforcement, direct provenance-door vs. transitive footprint exclusion test, illustrative Python 6-effect ceiling test admitting linked `py` recipe, non-empty `:trailing-requires` (`:module/require`) test, projected-name collision refusal, and 4-host prelude execution parity. |\n   804\t| **P1 — Layer 2a Tier 1 (`yrt.escape`, `yrt.float`, `yrt.int`)** | Implement the three stateless guest modules (frame indexing via `data/nth`, status-returning `yrt.float` boxed boundaries `neg-pow-result` / `floor-int-result` plus total `float-floor-raw` with zero raw-double callbacks and no `data/float64?` dependency); migrate `js`/`clj` from 4-slot to 5-slot contexts (`:handlers :depth :base :frame`); preserve open non-`:finally` (`:generator`) boundary dispatch; add `dsg__add`/`dsg__lte` helpers for bundled `clj`; activate across `py`, `js`, `php`, `clj`. | Refresh goldens cleanly | Unit tests for `yrt.*` on semantic/stack/register VMs; bundled/linked `yang.clojure` parity with source-defined `(defn get ...)` and active nested `try`/`throw`/`finally` frames; existing Python & PHP generator tests green; 4→5-slot migration tests; PHP `abandon-to` / `call-terminal` & normal `finally` replacement (`:py/None`, `:js/undefined`, `:php/null`, `nil`); `1.1 ** 6` bit-pattern parity (`fpow-half-raw` vs `fpow-base-raw`); exceptional `yrt.float` underflow (`0.5 ** -2000` -> `:yrt.float/underflow` + outer overflow policy), subnormal (`2.0 ** -1074` -> `5e-324`), normal zero (`2.0 ** -2000` -> `+0.0`), and out-of-range (`floor(1e30)`, `floor(NaN)`, `floor(Inf)`) witnesses under `%capture`/safepoints across 4 hosts; `yin.vm.integer` v4 three-reason translation without masking operational throws; independent concurrent `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj` tasks sharing `yrt.*`; bundled == linked + 4-host + CPython/Node/PHP oracle parity; `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` clean. |\n   805\t| **P2 — Lowering parameterization (`yang.core.semantics` + frontend contracts)** | Implement generic `yang.core.semantics` with UAST-derived arity & role validation against verified `:yin.module/tree` (`artifact-store`); define frontend contracts (Python, TypeScript, PHP, and `yang.clojure`, including uniform 2-arg `:unit/run-main [body-fn ambient-resolver]` and optional `:comp/finish`); refactor lowerings to read from `:yang.semantics/descriptor`. | Refresh goldens if ABI normalizes `run-main` | Full CPython/Node/PHP corpus + 4-host parity under default descriptors (`:yang.python/py-v1` keeping `:comp/finish nil`); capability tests (`:cell`, `:single-assignment`, `:ambient-only`); UAST-derived validation rejecting wrong arity, non-lambda hooks, wrong `:cell-accessor`/`:value` role, `:literals.*.overflow-op` defects, and exports outside the selected `:ambient-modules` closure; unqualified-hook & reserved-door (`*.impl/*`, `dsg__*`) rejection; refusal of typed `except E:` when `:control/except-typed :refused` and of generator expressions when `:control/generators :refused`. |\n   806\t| **P3 — Unified `clojure.core` + `yang.python/clojure-core-v1` + `yang.clojure` migration** | Add pure `data/float64?` (`yin.vm.data`) and `kind/namespace` (`yang.clojure/kind-module`); upgrade unified trusted Layer-2b `clj` (bundled & linked parity: two-step `make-callable`, evaluated `assoc` conditions, `invoke-callable`, `prim-get`/`prim-assoc`, retiring legacy `yang.clojure` `dsg__call_token` / inline provenance ops); publish collision-free `clojure.core.impl` (`impl-*` only) + cell-free `clojure.core` facade (`init!`, `export` using `clj/prim-get`, 0-arg accessors) and migrate `yang.clojure` onto them; publish `clj.py` + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`; wire `yang.frontend` multi-revision selection. | Refresh `clj` / `yang.clojure` goldens cleanly | 4-host numeric & `data/float64?` suite: `2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0`, `-0.0 // 2.0 == -0.0` (`data/content=`), `1.0 / 0.0` (`:zero-division`), `-(0.0)` (`-0.0`), `-(-0.0)` (`+0.0`), `2.0 + 1.0`, `2.0 * 3`, `5.0 - 2`, `inc(1.0)`, `2 ** -3`, negative/nonfinite `%`, fractional/infinite `**` refusal; minimum 53-bit floor (`:max-bits 53`) tests (`2.0 ** (2.0 ** 53)`, `rem` `:bit-limit` before `data/nth`, `integer/neg` bit-limit); uniform `admit-key!` across literals, `assoc`/`assoc_in`/`get`/`get_in`/`conj`/`contains?`/`disj`/`merge`/`into`/`union`/`difference`, and comprehensions refusing floats (`1.0`/`-0.0`/`NaN`/`[[-0.0]]`) AND ambiguous identifiers (`(keyword nil \"a/b\")`, `(symbol nil \"a/b\")`, `[(keyword nil \"a/b\")]`) as `:unsupported-key` on all 4 hosts while asserting `(keyword nil \"a/b\") == (keyword \"a\" \"b\") → false`; explicit equality assertions **`[0.0] == [-0.0] → true`**, **`{\"a\": -0.0} == {\"a\": 0.0} → true`**, **`[NaN] == [NaN] → false`**, **`{\"a\": NaN} == {\"a\": NaN} → false`**; linked `(clojure.core/identity)` & `(clojure.core/get)` (plus `assoc`, `conj`, `first`, `rest`, `nil?`, `empty?`, `not`, `vec`) end-to-end; authenticated callable cells returning **`false`** for `coll?`, `map?`, `set?`, `vector?`, `sequential?`, `seq?`, `list?`, `reduced?`, and `fn?` aligned 1-to-1 with `clj/invoke-callable`; two-step `make-callable` + evaluated `assoc` evidence asserting exact runtime `owner` & `:yang.call/binding-profile` at `raise-exit` (plus non-callable exit operational failure, ordinary binding error `:yang.call/thrown`, normal `20` preserved); two descriptors sharing the same `clj.py` address in one task mapping alias `\"op\"` to `inc` vs. `dec`; two importers sharing `(=)` cell in one task & isolated across two tasks; bundled == linked parity for nested `clj → clj.py → clj` unwinds over `(clj/rt-ctx)`; explicit canonical ordering witness (`keys` on mixed `nil`/bool/int/str/kw/symbol/vector/map/set) and 4-host deterministic `str`/`fresh-symbol`/`gensym`; nonempty list/set/dict comprehensions + bare `except:`; unified `yang.clojure` suite green. |\n   807\t| **P4 — Tier-2 shared modules & symmetric cross-frontend swapping** | Extract parameterized `yrt.gen` (preserving Python `:base` rebasing vs. PHP direct context restoration and refcount cleanup) and `yrt.safepoint` (`stream/poll!` skeleton for `pysp`/`jssp`); exercise symmetric cross-frontend swapping (such as compiling `yang.clojure` syntax onto Python runtime semantics via a `py.clj` adapter profile `:yang.clojure/py-v1`). | Refresh affected goldens cleanly | Generator + safepoint parity suites across VMs/hosts preserving PHP lifecycle/cleanup and non-rebasing context behavior vs. Python rebasing, plus bidirectional cross-frontend lowering parity test (`yang.python/clojure-core-v1` and `yang.clojure/py-v1`). |\n   808\t\n   809\t---\n   810\t\n   811\t## 10. Owner decisions and disposition ledger\n   812\t\n   813\t1. **D1 — Local mutation model for `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`:**\n   814\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* `:mutation/locals :cell` (task-heap cells holding pure persistent Clojure values, matching Python parameter binding, unbound reads, reassignment, loops, and `nonlocal` with per-module `globals` cells). Keep `:single-assignment` as a separate restricted profile.\n   815\t   - *Option B:* `:mutation/locals :single-assignment` only (refuses local reassignment).\n   816\t2. **D2 — Namespace prefix for Layer-2a shared modules:**\n   817\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* `yrt.*` (`yrt.escape`, `yrt.float`, `yrt.int`, `yrt.gen`, `yrt.safepoint`) matching `yang.typescript.md` §17 and `yang.php.md` §9, implemented in Clojure under `src/cljc/yang/rt/*.cljc`.\n   818\t   - *Option B:* `yang.rt.*` for both Clojure namespaces and linker module names.\n   819\t3. **D3 — Python float tagging during P1 (`:yang.python/py-v1` CPython equality oracle):**\n   820\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* Retain `{:py/float x}` behind a 2-line `py` boundary adapter around `yrt.float` through P1 so Python's `1 == 1.0` oracle semantics stay cleanly isolated while P1 extracts shared math.\n   821\t   - *Option B:* Migrate Python to untagged `data/float64` carriers in P1.\n   822\t4. **D4 — Golden migration policy (`Settled — Owner Clean-Slate Directive`):**\n   823\t   - Settled in favor of clean golden regeneration per slice (`P0` normalization, `P1` `yrt.*`, `P2` uniform `run-main`, `P3` unified `clj` / `clojure.core`), preserving correctness via behavioral, 4-host, and language-oracle suites rather than frozen-quirk backwards compatibility.\n   824\t5. **D5 — Cross-syntax identifier mapping for Clojure names (`?`, `!`, `-`):**\n   825\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* Curated `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` table validated against UAST-derived arity/roles, unit-bound `ambient-resolver`, lexical precedence, and reserved-door bans (`*.impl/*`, `dsg__*`).\n   826\t   - *Option B:* Algorithmic mangling rule (`_q` / `_bang`).\n   827\t6. **D6 — Publishing `clojure.core` and migrating `yang.clojure` (`Settled — Owner Clean-Slate Directive`):**\n   828\t   - Settled in favor of publishing collision-free `clojure.core.impl` + cell-free `clojure.core` AND migrating `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core` in P3 (retiring `yang.clojure`'s legacy `library-for` duplication and unit-local `dsg__call_token` path so there is one unified Clojure runtime).\n   829\t7. **D7 — Float exponentiation rounding (`py`/`js` half-power vs. `php` base squaring):**\n   830\t   - *Option A (Recommended for P1 — Architect concurred):* Export both `yrt.float/fpow-half-raw` (selected by `:half` in `neg-pow-result`) and `yrt.float/fpow-base-raw` (selected by `:base`) so P1 preserves bit-exact parity (`1.1 ** 6`: `0x1.c585058dde7acp+0` for `py`/`js` vs `0x1.c585058dde7abp+0` for `php`) across existing CPython/Node and PHP language oracles.\n   831\t   - *Option B:* Explicitly approve unifying PHP onto `fpow-half-raw` (or `py`/`js` onto `fpow-base-raw`) and update the affected language's oracle departure ledger.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
