{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '635,650p;688,746p;795,831p'\"","aggregated_output":"   635\t| `:unit/run-main` | `[body-fn ambient-resolver]` | Calls idempotent `(clj/init!)`, `(clojure.core/init!)`, and `(clj.py/init!)` (where `clj.py` exports idempotent 0-arg `init!`, 1-arg `export` via `clj/prim-get`, and 0-arg cell-accessor `ex-info`, satisfying `§6.4`'s `:cell-accessor` contract); allocates a **fresh per-unit `globals` cell** `(cell/new (assoc (assoc {} :vars {}) :ambient ambient-resolver))` and `globals-fn`; invokes `(body-fn globals globals-fn)` inside a top-level handler on `(clj/rt-ctx)`; returns the value **verbatim without stripping `[:yin.k/ok ...]`** so ordinary Python data shaped like `[:yin.k/ok 42]` passes through uncorrupted. |\n   636\t\n   637\t*(Lowerings with `:mutation/locals :single-assignment` remain a separate, stricter profile variant that omits local variable cells and refuses assignment/reassignment to locals, loops with mutated accumulators, and `nonlocal`.)*\n   638\t\n   639\t### 7.4 Unified trusted `clj` callable bridge, cross-unit admission, and §8.10.7 validation\n   640\t\n   641\tBecause `yang.call/eligible?` (`src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc:29–48`) only dereferences authenticated cell-refs and leaves ordinary maps intact, structural eligibility alone does **not** stop source-constructed maps carrying `:yang.call/entry` from masquerading as callables when source maps are first-class data. Under the Owner Clean-Slate Directive (no legacy runtime retention needed), all Clojure-family §8.10.7 callable/provenance bridging is unified directly into **trusted Layer-2b `clj`** (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc`, requiring `yang.call` and `yrt.escape`) — eliminating both any separate `clj.bridge` module AND `yang.clojure`'s legacy `dsg__call_token` / inline provenance code in P3!\n   642\t\n   643\t- `clj` owns the private provenance doors (`cell/dsg__new-provenance`, `cell/dsg__provenance`) inside **both** its linked (`module-uast`) and bundled (`uast`) emitters (preserving §5.2 Bundled vs. Linked Parity Law!), never exporting them and keeping them strictly out of `yrt.*`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core.impl`, and `clojure.core`.\n   644\t- `clj` also exports collision-free primitive helpers **`clj/prim-get`** (`(fn [m k] (get m k))`) and **`clj/prim-assoc`** (`(fn [m k v] (assoc m k v))`) — safe inside `clj` because `clj` has zero stripped exports named `get` or `assoc` in its module store (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:62–175`).\n   645\t\n   646\t`clj` enforces the full §8.10 + §8.10.7 contract:\n   647\t\n   648\t1. **Source-level callable admission (`clj/admitted-callable?`):**\n   649\t   - Called by `clj/invoke-callable`, `clj.py/callable?`, `clojure.core.impl/impl-fn?`, and `clojure.core.impl`'s dynamic higher-order caller **before** invoking `yang.call/invoke`. Written strictly in prelude special-form notation (`src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc:82` — nested `if`, zero `and` form!):\n   650\t     ```clojure\n   688\t     ```\n   689\t   - **Step D — Value-returning boundary (`yrt.escape/try-value` — NOT `try-orelse`!) around binding + body:**\n   690\t     - Installs the exception handler on `(clj/rt-ctx)` **before** argument binding so ordinary named-arg / positional-arity errors share the same boundary: inside `try-value`, `(bind-and-run positional named)` checks `:yang.call/named` and positional/varargs arity against `:spec` (raising local guest binding exceptions via `clj/raise` so they cross under **`:yang.call/thrown`**) and evaluates the body.\n   691\t     - On normal completion, `yrt.escape/try-value` restores `(clj/rt-ctx)` and returns the body's value verbatim (`20` in §7.6).\n   692\t     - On escape with `e`, the handler inspects private `(cell/dsg__provenance e)`: if non-nil (an authentic retained protocol condition from a deeper cross-language boundary), forwards that retained condition **directly** to `raise-exit` without double-wrapping; otherwise wraps `e` (including condition-shaped user maps!) via `(yang.call/thrown e)` and transfers it to `raise-exit`.\n   693\t4. **Call-site boundary (`clj/invoke-callable`):**\n   694\t   - Validates `(clj/admitted-callable? callee)`; if false, mints private retained `:yang.call/not-callable` via `cell/dsg__new-provenance` (with evaluated `(assoc {} :yang.call/callee callee)` evidence) and raises on `(clj/rt-ctx)`.\n   695\t   - Otherwise calls `yang.call/invoke` with a dedicated `raise-exit` closure:\n   696\t     - If `(= (get condition :yang.call/reason) :yang.call/thrown)`, calls `(clj/raise (get condition :yang.call/value))` (unwrapping user-thrown values).\n   697\t     - Otherwise retains the protocol condition inside a private provenance carrier `(clj/raise (cell/dsg__new-provenance condition condition))`, preserving full condition fidelity across `A → B → A` unwinds and `finally` blocks, as well as nested `clj → clj.py → clj` unwinding on `(clj/rt-ctx)`.\n   698\t\n   699\t### 7.5 Two-module portable `clojure.core` contract (`clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core`)\n   700\t\n   701\tIn Slice P3, the portable Clojure standard library is split cleanly into two complementary Layer-2c linker modules — eliminating **all** store-key collisions against VM primitives (`src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:116`, `src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc:42`) while publishing cell-free 0-arg export accessors (`src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:915, 1055`):\n   702\t\n   703\t1. **`clojure.core.impl` (pure, stateless implementation module — banned from `:ambient-projections`):**\n   704\t   - Requires `yang.call`, `clj`, `yrt.float`, `yrt.int` (zero direct provenance doors; zero state cells).\n   705\t   - Registered host dependencies: `kind` (with `:pure` `kind/namespace`), `data` (with `:pure` `data/float64?`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), and `cell` (for cell checks/updates only; zero module state).\n   706\t   - **Zero bare primitive store collisions:** EVERY definition inside `clojure.core.impl` is named **`impl-<op>`** (`impl-identity`, `impl-get`, `impl-assoc`, `impl-conj`, `impl-first`, `impl-rest`, `impl-seq`, `impl-vec`, `impl-nil?`, `impl-empty?`, `impl-not`, `impl-map`, etc.)! Because NO store key in `clojure.core.impl` is named `get`, `assoc`, `conj`, `first`, `rest`, `vec`, `nil?`, `empty?`, `not`, or `=`, every internal call to `(get m k)`, `(assoc m k v)`, `(conj xs x)`, `(first xs)`, `(rest xs)`, `(vec xs)`, `(nil? x)`, `(empty? xs)`, `(not b)` resolves straight to the VM primitive!\n   707\t2. **Audited observable operations inside `clojure.core.impl` (eliminating all host leaks):**\n   708\t   - **Pure non-numeric definitions:** `impl-identity`, `impl-second`, `impl-boolean?`, `impl-count`, `impl-symbol?`, `impl-keyword?`, `impl-meta`, `impl-name`, `impl-symbol`, `impl-keyword`, `impl-last`, `impl-butlast`, `impl-string?`, `impl-with-meta`, `impl-set?`, `impl-reverse`, `impl-cons`, `impl-list`, `impl-vector`, `impl-reduced`, `impl-unreduced`, `impl-concat`.\n   709\t   - **Cell-safe collection predicates (fixing handle misclassification):**\n   710\t     - `impl-cell-ref? [x]` (nested `if`: `(if (data/map? x) (if (= (get x :type) :cell-ref) (cell/authentic? x) false) false)`).\n   711\t     - `impl-coll? [x]`: returns `false` if `(impl-cell-ref? x)`, else `(kind/coll? x)`.\n   712\t     - `impl-map? [x]`: returns `false` if `(impl-cell-ref? x)`, else `(data/map? x)`.\n   713\t     - `impl-reduced? [x]`: returns `false` if `(impl-cell-ref? x)`, else `(if (nil? x) false (= true (get x :yin.k/reduced)))`.\n   714\t     - `impl-vector? [x]`: `(data/vector? x)`.\n   715\t     - Because `impl-sequential? [x]` uses `(if (impl-coll? x) (if (impl-map? x) false (not (kind/set? x))) false)` and `impl-seq?` / `impl-list?` delegate to `impl-sequential?`, **an authenticated callable cell answers `false` to ALL of `coll?`, `map?`, `set?`, `vector?`, `sequential?`, `seq?`, `list?`, and `reduced?`!**\n   716\t   - **Numeric & equality rewrites:**\n   717\t     - `impl-inc`, `impl-dec`: `integer/integer?` → `integer/add`/`integer/sub` + `yrt.int/check-limit`; `data/float64?` → leaf unwrap ± `(data/float-value 1)` + `data/float64`; non-numeric → guest type error via `clj/raise`.\n   718\t     - `impl-rem`: validates `(if (integer/integer? a) (integer/integer? b) false)` and `b != 0`, binds **`qr = (yrt.int/check-limit (integer/quot-rem a b) ...)` BEFORE calling `(data/nth qr 1)`**.\n   719\t     - `impl-not=`: delegates to `(not (impl-eq a b))` (`§7.2`: exact `integer/compare`, leaf float `-0.0 == 0.0` / `NaN != NaN`, kind-strict `1 != 1.0`, namespace+name identifiers, recursive collection equality).\n   720\t     - `impl-int?`: `integer/integer?`.\n   721\t     - `impl-fn?`: **identical to `clj/admitted-callable?`** (nested `if`, strictly authenticated cell-backed `yang.call` callables — zero `(data/callable? x)` fallback).\n   722\t     - `impl-fresh-symbol`, `impl-gensym`: validate integer counter via `integer/integer?`, increment via `integer/add` + `yrt.int/check-limit`, format via `integer/format` + `yrt.int/check-limit`, concatenate via `data/str-concat`.\n   723\t     - `impl-str`: explicit 4-host deterministic renderer (`nil -> \"\"`; strings verbatim; booleans `\"true\"`/`\"false\"`; exact ints via `integer/format` + `yrt.int/check-limit`; `data/float64?` via leaf unwrap + `integer/float-digits` + `yrt.float/{zeros,exp-text}` with explicit `\"NaN\"`, `\"Infinity\"`, `\"-Infinity\"`, `\"0.0\"`, `\"-0.0\"`, printing `1.0 -> \"1.0\"`; keywords/symbols via `kind/namespace` + `kind/name`; vectors/lists recursively; maps/sets in `canonical-compare` order; authenticated cells as `\"#<fn>\"`).\n   724\t   - **Complete deterministic `canonical-compare` over admitted `v1` keys & elements:**\n   725\t     - Helper `cmp-opt-str [a b]`: `(nil, nil) -> 0`, `(nil, non-nil) -> -1`, `(non-nil, nil) -> 1`, `(str, str) -> (data/str-compare a b)` (never passing `nil` into `data/str-compare` at `yin/vm/data.cljc:396`!).\n   726\t     - Distinct type ranks: `0: nil`, `1: boolean (false < true)`, `2: exact integer (integer/compare)`, `3: string (data/str-compare)`, `4: keyword (cmp-opt-str ns, then data/str-compare name)`, `5: symbol (cmp-opt-str ns, then data/str-compare name)`, `6: vector`, `7: map`, `8: set`.\n   727\t     - **Within-kind compound lexicographic rules:**\n   728\t       - **Vector:** compare elementwise at indices `0 .. min(na, nb) - 1` via `canonical-compare`; if all shared elements tie, compare `(integer/compare na nb)`.\n   729\t       - **Map:** canonicalize each map's `[k v]` entry vector sorted ascending by `canonical-compare` on `k`; compare the two sorted `[k v]` entry vectors lexicographically (comparing `k` via `canonical-compare`, then `v` via `canonical-compare`, then entry count).\n   730\t       - **Set:** canonicalize each set into a vector of elements sorted ascending by `canonical-compare`; compare via the vector rule above.\n   731\t     - `impl-seq`, `impl-first`, `impl-rest`, `impl-vec`, `impl-keys`, `impl-vals`, `impl-str`, `impl-reduce`, `impl-map`, `impl-filter`, `impl-remove`, `impl-into`, `impl-merge`, `impl-union`, and `impl-difference` all normalize map entry pairs and set elements via `canonical-compare` before ordered traversal.\n   732\t     - `impl-nth`: validates index via `integer/integer?`, checks bounds via `integer/compare`, and restricts to sequential collections (`impl-sequential?` / `data/vector?`).\n   733\t     - **Uniform `admit-key!`:** enforced on `impl-assoc`, `impl-assoc-in`, `impl-update`, `impl-update-in`, `impl-get`, `impl-get-in`, `impl-contains?`, `impl-conj` (on maps/sets), `impl-disj`, `impl-merge`, `impl-into` (targeting maps/sets), `impl-union`, `impl-difference`, `impl-hash-map`, `impl-set`, `impl-get-coll`, `impl-assoc-coll`, `impl-conj-coll`.\n   734\t     - **Explicitly excluded:** `var?`, `resolve`, and `invoke-value`.\n   735\t3. **Public cell-free facade `clojure.core` (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/core_module.cljc`):**\n   736\t   - Requires **`clj`** and **`clojure.core.impl`**. Exports ONLY cell-free pure functions at install time (`src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:915, 1055`):\n   737\t     1. Internal non-exported runtime placeholders `clojure.core.rt/state` and `clojure.core.rt/exports` start at `:clojure.core/uninit`.\n   738\t     2. **`clojure.core/init!` (`[]`):** Idempotent per-task initializer — checks `(= clojure.core.rt/state :clojure.core/uninit)` (safe because `=` is not exported by `clojure.core`), calls `(clj/init!)`, builds `{sym cell}` using **`clj/prim-assoc`** (NEVER bare `assoc`!) and `(clj/make-callable meta wrapper-for-impl-*)` for every public export (`identity`, `inc`, `dec`, `str`, `count`, `first`, `rest`, `second`, `cons`, `conj`, `assoc`, `assoc-in`, `get`, `get-in`, `update`, `update-in`, `map`, `filter`, `reduce`, `into`, `keys`, `vals`, `merge`, `empty?`, `nil?`, `map?`, `vector?`, `set?`, etc.), stores it via `(yin/def (quote clojure.core.rt/exports) (cell/new export-map))`, and flips `(yin/def (quote clojure.core.rt/state) :clojure.core/ready)`.\n   739\t     3. **`clojure.core/export` (`[sym]`):** Calls `(clojure.core/init!)` and returns **`(clj/prim-get (cell/get clojure.core.rt/exports) sym)`** — using qualified `clj/prim-get` so looking up `sym` NEVER recurses into `clojure.core`'s stripped `get` store entry! Two importers in one task receive the identical (`=`) cell; two tasks receive isolated cells.\n   740\t     4. **Public 0-arg cell-accessor exports:** For every public library function `<name>`, `clojure.core` exports `(fn [] (clojure.core/export (quote <name>)))`. Because zero `:cell-ref` values exist in `:slice`, `lift-slice` succeeds uniformly across all 4 hosts, `validate-descriptor` verifies the 0-arg `:lambda` shape directly in `clojure.core`'s verified UAST tree, and callers obtain the stable task-local cell by calling `(clojure.core/<name>)`.\n   741\t   - **Dynamic closure construction & internal call discipline:**\n   742\t     - Closures returned at runtime by `impl-comp` and `impl-partial` are constructed via **`clj/make-callable`** (preserving cross-unit authenticated cell identity `=`), static sibling calls inside `clojure.core.impl` invoke stripped `impl-*` lambdas directly, and all dynamic callbacks (`f` in `impl-map`, `impl-filter`, `impl-remove`, `impl-reduce`, `impl-update`, `impl-update-in`, `impl-comp`, `impl-partial`) go exclusively through **`clj/invoke-callable`**.\n   743\t4. **No implicit namespace dump & clean unification of `yang.clojure` in P3:**\n   744\t   - Adding `'clojure.core` to `:requires` exposes nothing to user code on its own; only explicit entries in `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` enter source scope.\n   745\t   - Under the Owner Clean-Slate Directive, **Slice P3 migrates `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core`** (retiring `yang.clojure`'s old inline `library-for` duplication, unit-local `dsg__call_token` admission, and inline provenance ops cleanly — zero dual stdlib!).\n   746\t\n   795\t- Whenever prelude normalization (`P0` uniform `:trailing-requires` / `:finalize-c1?`), runtime extraction (`P1` `yrt.*`), uniform Hook ABI signatures (`P2` 2-arg `:unit/run-main`), or Clojure stdlib unification (`P3`) changes emitted bytes, regenerate affected golden snapshots cleanly and validate correctness via behavioral, 4-host, and language-oracle parity suites.\n   796\t\n   797\t---\n   798\t\n   799\t## 9. Phased implementation roadmap and acceptance gates\n   800\t\n   801\t| Slice | Scope & deliverables | Golden impact | Concrete acceptance gate |\n   802\t|---|---|---|---|\n   803\t| **P0 — Uniform composition plumbing & `defquoted` consolidation** | Consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.prelude`; implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` (with independent `:components`, explicit `:trailing-requires`, uniform `:finalize-c1? true`) / `:yang.prelude/profile`, `validate-profile` (direct `:yin.module/primitives`/`:exports` provenance ban vs. transitive `:yin.module/footprint` ceiling; verified `:yin.module/tree` closure), and `admit-profile` (explicit `host-limits`); standardize `py`, `js`, `php`, `clj`, `yang.call` base preludes (`:trailing-requires []`, `:finalize-c1? true`; safepoint overlays keep explicit `:trailing-requires ['py]` / `['js]`). | Regenerate `py`/`php`/`py.sp` cleanly | Direct-vs.-transitive `:requires` closure tests (including transitive-only deps), missing manifest/`:yin.module/tree` refusal, `host-limits` numeric-floor enforcement, direct provenance-door vs. transitive footprint exclusion test, illustrative Python 6-effect ceiling test admitting linked `py` recipe, non-empty `:trailing-requires` (`:module/require`) test, projected-name collision refusal, and 4-host prelude execution parity. |\n   804\t| **P1 — Layer 2a Tier 1 (`yrt.escape`, `yrt.float`, `yrt.int`)** | Implement the three stateless guest modules (frame indexing via `data/nth`, status-returning `yrt.float` boxed boundaries `neg-pow-result` / `floor-int-result` plus total `float-floor-raw` with zero raw-double callbacks and no `data/float64?` dependency); migrate `js`/`clj` from 4-slot to 5-slot contexts (`:handlers :depth :base :frame`); preserve open non-`:finally` (`:generator`) boundary dispatch; add `dsg__add`/`dsg__lte` helpers for bundled `clj`; activate across `py`, `js`, `php`, `clj`. | Refresh goldens cleanly | Unit tests for `yrt.*` on semantic/stack/register VMs; bundled/linked `yang.clojure` parity with source-defined `(defn get ...)` and active nested `try`/`throw`/`finally` frames; existing Python & PHP generator tests green; 4→5-slot migration tests; PHP `abandon-to` / `call-terminal` & normal `finally` replacement (`:py/None`, `:js/undefined`, `:php/null`, `nil`); `1.1 ** 6` bit-pattern parity (`fpow-half-raw` vs `fpow-base-raw`); exceptional `yrt.float` underflow (`0.5 ** -2000` -> `:yrt.float/underflow` + outer overflow policy), subnormal (`2.0 ** -1074` -> `5e-324`), normal zero (`2.0 ** -2000` -> `+0.0`), and out-of-range (`floor(1e30)`, `floor(NaN)`, `floor(Inf)`) witnesses under `%capture`/safepoints across 4 hosts; `yin.vm.integer` v4 three-reason translation without masking operational throws; independent concurrent `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj` tasks sharing `yrt.*`; bundled == linked + 4-host + CPython/Node/PHP oracle parity; `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` clean. |\n   805\t| **P2 — Lowering parameterization (`yang.core.semantics` + frontend contracts)** | Implement generic `yang.core.semantics` with UAST-derived arity & role validation against verified `:yin.module/tree` (`artifact-store`); define frontend contracts (Python, TypeScript, PHP, and `yang.clojure`, including uniform 2-arg `:unit/run-main [body-fn ambient-resolver]` and optional `:comp/finish`); refactor lowerings to read from `:yang.semantics/descriptor`. | Refresh goldens if ABI normalizes `run-main` | Full CPython/Node/PHP corpus + 4-host parity under default descriptors (`:yang.python/py-v1` keeping `:comp/finish nil`); capability tests (`:cell`, `:single-assignment`, `:ambient-only`); UAST-derived validation rejecting wrong arity, non-lambda hooks, wrong `:cell-accessor`/`:value` role, `:literals.*.overflow-op` defects, and exports outside the selected `:ambient-modules` closure; unqualified-hook & reserved-door (`*.impl/*`, `dsg__*`) rejection; refusal of typed `except E:` when `:control/except-typed :refused` and of generator expressions when `:control/generators :refused`. |\n   806\t| **P3 — Unified `clojure.core` + `yang.python/clojure-core-v1` + `yang.clojure` migration** | Add pure `data/float64?` (`yin.vm.data`) and `kind/namespace` (`yang.clojure/kind-module`); upgrade unified trusted Layer-2b `clj` (bundled & linked parity: two-step `make-callable`, evaluated `assoc` conditions, `invoke-callable`, `prim-get`/`prim-assoc`, retiring legacy `yang.clojure` `dsg__call_token` / inline provenance ops); publish collision-free `clojure.core.impl` (`impl-*` only) + cell-free `clojure.core` facade (`init!`, `export` using `clj/prim-get`, 0-arg accessors) and migrate `yang.clojure` onto them; publish `clj.py` + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`; wire `yang.frontend` multi-revision selection. | Refresh `clj` / `yang.clojure` goldens cleanly | 4-host numeric & `data/float64?` suite: `2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0`, `-0.0 // 2.0 == -0.0` (`data/content=`), `1.0 / 0.0` (`:zero-division`), `-(0.0)` (`-0.0`), `-(-0.0)` (`+0.0`), `2.0 + 1.0`, `2.0 * 3`, `5.0 - 2`, `inc(1.0)`, `2 ** -3`, negative/nonfinite `%`, fractional/infinite `**` refusal; minimum 53-bit floor (`:max-bits 53`) tests (`2.0 ** (2.0 ** 53)`, `rem` `:bit-limit` before `data/nth`, `integer/neg` bit-limit); uniform `admit-key!` across literals, `assoc`/`assoc_in`/`get`/`get_in`/`conj`/`contains?`/`disj`/`merge`/`into`/`union`/`difference`, and comprehensions refusing floats (`1.0`/`-0.0`/`NaN`/`[[-0.0]]`) AND ambiguous identifiers (`(keyword nil \"a/b\")`, `(symbol nil \"a/b\")`, `[(keyword nil \"a/b\")]`) as `:unsupported-key` on all 4 hosts while asserting `(keyword nil \"a/b\") == (keyword \"a\" \"b\") → false`; explicit equality assertions **`[0.0] == [-0.0] → true`**, **`{\"a\": -0.0} == {\"a\": 0.0} → true`**, **`[NaN] == [NaN] → false`**, **`{\"a\": NaN} == {\"a\": NaN} → false`**; linked `(clojure.core/identity)` & `(clojure.core/get)` (plus `assoc`, `conj`, `first`, `rest`, `nil?`, `empty?`, `not`, `vec`) end-to-end; authenticated callable cells returning **`false`** for `coll?`, `map?`, `set?`, `vector?`, `sequential?`, `seq?`, `list?`, `reduced?`, and `fn?` aligned 1-to-1 with `clj/invoke-callable`; two-step `make-callable` + evaluated `assoc` evidence asserting exact runtime `owner` & `:yang.call/binding-profile` at `raise-exit` (plus non-callable exit operational failure, ordinary binding error `:yang.call/thrown`, normal `20` preserved); two descriptors sharing the same `clj.py` address in one task mapping alias `\"op\"` to `inc` vs. `dec`; two importers sharing `(=)` cell in one task & isolated across two tasks; bundled == linked parity for nested `clj → clj.py → clj` unwinds over `(clj/rt-ctx)`; explicit canonical ordering witness (`keys` on mixed `nil`/bool/int/str/kw/symbol/vector/map/set) and 4-host deterministic `str`/`fresh-symbol`/`gensym`; nonempty list/set/dict comprehensions + bare `except:`; unified `yang.clojure` suite green. |\n   807\t| **P4 — Tier-2 shared modules & symmetric cross-frontend swapping** | Extract parameterized `yrt.gen` (preserving Python `:base` rebasing vs. PHP direct context restoration and refcount cleanup) and `yrt.safepoint` (`stream/poll!` skeleton for `pysp`/`jssp`); exercise symmetric cross-frontend swapping (such as compiling `yang.clojure` syntax onto Python runtime semantics via a `py.clj` adapter profile `:yang.clojure/py-v1`). | Refresh affected goldens cleanly | Generator + safepoint parity suites across VMs/hosts preserving PHP lifecycle/cleanup and non-rebasing context behavior vs. Python rebasing, plus bidirectional cross-frontend lowering parity test (`yang.python/clojure-core-v1` and `yang.clojure/py-v1`). |\n   808\t\n   809\t---\n   810\t\n   811\t## 10. Owner decisions and disposition ledger\n   812\t\n   813\t1. **D1 — Local mutation model for `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`:**\n   814\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* `:mutation/locals :cell` (task-heap cells holding pure persistent Clojure values, matching Python parameter binding, unbound reads, reassignment, loops, and `nonlocal` with per-module `globals` cells). Keep `:single-assignment` as a separate restricted profile.\n   815\t   - *Option B:* `:mutation/locals :single-assignment` only (refuses local reassignment).\n   816\t2. **D2 — Namespace prefix for Layer-2a shared modules:**\n   817\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* `yrt.*` (`yrt.escape`, `yrt.float`, `yrt.int`, `yrt.gen`, `yrt.safepoint`) matching `yang.typescript.md` §17 and `yang.php.md` §9, implemented in Clojure under `src/cljc/yang/rt/*.cljc`.\n   818\t   - *Option B:* `yang.rt.*` for both Clojure namespaces and linker module names.\n   819\t3. **D3 — Python float tagging during P1 (`:yang.python/py-v1` CPython equality oracle):**\n   820\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* Retain `{:py/float x}` behind a 2-line `py` boundary adapter around `yrt.float` through P1 so Python's `1 == 1.0` oracle semantics stay cleanly isolated while P1 extracts shared math.\n   821\t   - *Option B:* Migrate Python to untagged `data/float64` carriers in P1.\n   822\t4. **D4 — Golden migration policy (`Settled — Owner Clean-Slate Directive`):**\n   823\t   - Settled in favor of clean golden regeneration per slice (`P0` normalization, `P1` `yrt.*`, `P2` uniform `run-main`, `P3` unified `clj` / `clojure.core`), preserving correctness via behavioral, 4-host, and language-oracle suites rather than frozen-quirk backwards compatibility.\n   824\t5. **D5 — Cross-syntax identifier mapping for Clojure names (`?`, `!`, `-`):**\n   825\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* Curated `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` table validated against UAST-derived arity/roles, unit-bound `ambient-resolver`, lexical precedence, and reserved-door bans (`*.impl/*`, `dsg__*`).\n   826\t   - *Option B:* Algorithmic mangling rule (`_q` / `_bang`).\n   827\t6. **D6 — Publishing `clojure.core` and migrating `yang.clojure` (`Settled — Owner Clean-Slate Directive`):**\n   828\t   - Settled in favor of publishing collision-free `clojure.core.impl` + cell-free `clojure.core` AND migrating `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core` in P3 (retiring `yang.clojure`'s legacy `library-for` duplication and unit-local `dsg__call_token` path so there is one unified Clojure runtime).\n   829\t7. **D7 — Float exponentiation rounding (`py`/`js` half-power vs. `php` base squaring):**\n   830\t   - *Option A (Recommended for P1 — Architect concurred):* Export both `yrt.float/fpow-half-raw` (selected by `:half` in `neg-pow-result`) and `yrt.float/fpow-base-raw` (selected by `:base`) so P1 preserves bit-exact parity (`1.1 ** 6`: `0x1.c585058dde7acp+0` for `py`/`js` vs `0x1.c585058dde7abp+0` for `php`) across existing CPython/Node and PHP language oracles.\n   831\t   - *Option B:* Explicitly approve unifying PHP onto `fpow-half-raw` (or `py`/`js` onto `fpow-base-raw`) and update the affected language's oracle departure ledger.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
