{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '60,86p;285,300p'\nrg -n 'require|preload|install' docs/design/yang.preludes.md | cut -c1-230 | tail -43\"","aggregated_output":"    60\t1. **Everything is a Stream:** Prelude selection, composition, and lowering are pure functions of explicit data configurations and CST streams. Any external effect a prelude needs (`stream/put!`, `stream/poll!`, host I/O) remains a declared Layer-4 effect in the module manifest; prelude composition adds no ambient I/O.\n    61\t2. **Interpretation Creates Semantics:** A CST packet carries syntax only; its runtime meaning emerges from the tuple `(cst-packet, lowering-profile, semantics-descriptor, runtime-profile)`. Interpreting one Python CST under `:yang.python/py-v1` (CPython semantics) versus `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (Clojure persistent-data semantics) is a direct realization of \"one truth, many perspectives.\"\n    62\t3. **Code and State are Datoms (and Unitarity / Derive-Don't-Persist):**\n    63\t   - Lowering preserves source CST identity; compiled UAST roots under different preludes have distinct content addresses (or identical addresses when two descriptors emit identical UAST) linked by explicit provenance datoms pinning `(cst-address, lowering-profile, semantics-descriptor, runtime-profile, unit-address)`.\n    64\t   - Zero new AST tags, zero VM opcodes, and zero manifest schema changes are introduced. Linker manifests retain schema 1, and C1 `:yang/call-site` tables continue to publish beside manifests rather than inside them.\n    65\t   - Composition facts (which `yrt.*` modules a prelude requires) live in the explicit module `:requires` DAG, never as a redundant tag in UAST rows.\n    66\t4. **Everything is a Continuation:** Shared control-flow primitives (`yrt.escape`) and coroutine stepping (`yrt.gen`) remain pure guest UAST over `%capture` and task-heap cells (`cell/*`).\n    67\t\n    68\t### 2.2 Non-negotiable invariants\n    69\t\n    70\t1. **No hidden global state — stateless `yrt.*` modules:**\n    71\t   - `yang.core.*` holds no mutable global registry of preludes or languages (`yang.frontend` immutable catalog rule).\n    72\t   - **Shared `yrt.*` modules own zero `*.rt/*` state cells.** Every stateful `yrt.*` function takes the caller's task-local state cell (e.g., `ctx-cell`) as an explicit parameter. When a single Yin task links independent foreign language runtimes (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj`) together via `yang.call`, each foreign runtime maintains its own isolated handler stack and depth/base accounting inside its own `*.rt/ctx` cell rather than aliasing or corrupting another language's stack.\n    73\t   - **Intentional intra-Clojure domain sharing:** By explicit architectural design, `clj`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core.impl`, and `clojure.core` execute *inside* the Clojure semantics and exception domain and therefore share `(clj/rt-ctx)` intentionally so Clojure `(throw ...)` / `(try ... (finally ...))` and Python-syntax `try` / `except` / `finally` unwind across `clj → clj.py → clj` nesting on one coherent handler stack while saving and restoring `(clj/rt-ctx)` at every `yrt.escape/try-value` and `finally` boundary.\n    74\t2. **No implicit control flow:** All escapes remain explicit continuation invocations over an explicit handler chain.\n    75\t3. **No raw callbacks:** Policy hooks passed by a language prelude into `yrt.*` (`on-empty`, `on-range`, `on-underflow`, `on-bit-limit`, `on-digit-limit`, `on-float-overflow`, `fin`) are ordinary guest Yin closures, never host-boundary callbacks.\n    76\t4. **No shared mutable state:** Each stateful profile allocates its own task-local cells once per task in its own idempotent `init!` under its own private namespace (`py.rt/*`, `js.rt/*`, `php.rt/*`, `clj.rt/*`, `clj.py.rt/*`, `clojure.core.rt/*`); `clojure.core.impl` is pure and stateless.\n    77\t5. **No layer collapsing:** Parsing (host ANTLR boundary) → lowering (syntax + frontend lowering contract + semantics descriptor → UAST) → prelude composition & admission (pure spec/artifact verification; never publishes or executes) → publication/linking → VM execution stay separated across explicit stream/module boundaries.\n    78\t6. **No assumed graphs:** Every composed prelude declares an explicit, acyclic `:requires` DAG over an **immutable, verified artifact closure**. Missing exports, missing transitive artifacts, or cycles fail closed at validation/admission time before publication or execution.\n    79\t7. **No closed language registry (`yang.antlr.md` owner directive):** Neither `yrt.*` nor `yang.core.*` contains a `case`/dispatch over `:python`, `:typescript`, `:php`, or `:clojure`, inspects `:py/type`/`:js/type`/`:php/type`/`:clj/type` tags, or encodes language-specific lowering ABI tables.\n    80\t8. **Security boundary — VM provenance doors stay private:** Under `src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md` and `src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc`, `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and `cell/dsg__provenance` are reserved compiler/runtime-module doors whose names guest code must not forge or re-export.\n    81\t   - **`yrt.*` modules, `clj.py`, and Layer-2c standard libraries (`clojure.core.impl`, `clojure.core`) MUST NEVER declare (`:yin.module/primitives`) or export (`:yin.module/exports`) provenance-door primitives directly.** (Note that when a module such as `clojure.core` requires trusted Layer-2b `clj`, `yin.vm.linker.publish/footprint` legitimately unions `clj`'s `:cell/new-provenance` / `:cell/provenance` effects transitively into `:yin.module/footprint`; security exclusion is therefore checked directly on each module's `:yin.module/primitives` and `:yin.module/exports`, while transitive `:yin.module/footprint` is governed by `:yang.prelude/max-effects`.)\n    82\t   - **No descriptor hook or source-facing ambient projection** may expose `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, `yang.safepoint/*`, or non-projectable internal implementation modules such as `*.impl/*` (`clojure.core.impl/*`) (`§6.3`).\n    83\t   - Retained protocol-condition provenance (`yang.antlr.md` §8.10.7) resides strictly inside trusted Layer-2b runtime modules (`py`, `js`, `php`, **`clj`**) in **both** bundled (`uast`) and linked (`module-uast`) emission, never exported and never exposed across `yrt.*`, Layer-2c libraries, or source scope.\n    84\t\n    85\t---\n    86\t\n   285\t    {:cell {:required true}\n   286\t     :data {:required true, :min-max-items 1048576}\n   287\t     :integer {:required true, :min-bits 53}}\n   288\t    :yang.prelude/max-effects nil} ;; optional allowed-effect ceiling: for standardized linked `py` (`:trailing-requires []`), the verified footprint is `#{:cell/new :cell/get :cell/set! :cell/authentic? :cell/new-provenance :cell/provenance}` (recipes with non-empty `:trailing-requires` such as `py.sp`/`js.sp` also include `:module/require`); `nil` = derive from verified closure without an extra ceiling\n   289\t   ```\n   290\t   A `:yang.prelude/profile` contains zero host functions or closures and passes `yang.frontend/non-portable-path`. Its `:yang.prelude/root-address` ensures two profiles cannot claim identical identity while pointing at different owning prelude definitions.\n   291\t\n   292\t### 5.2 Composition rules and verified-closure admission\n   293\t\n   294\t`yang.core.prelude` and `yang.core.prelude-admission` enforce six fail-closed checks:\n   295\t\n   296\t1. **Verified artifact closure input (`validate-profile`):**\n   297\t   - Admission takes `(profile artifact-store registry)`, where `artifact-store` supplies an **immutable, verified content-addressed map** of published manifests (`manifest-addr -> verified-manifest`) AND their referenced canonical module trees (`tree-addr -> verified-uast`) — never assuming a graph from bare `[sym addr]` pairs!\n   298\t   - Separately checks **direct root pins** and the **transitive closure**:\n   299\t     - Every `[sym addr]` in `:yang.prelude/components` and `:yang.prelude/root-address` resolves in `artifact-store`, and the root manifest's direct `:requires` map matches `:yang.prelude/components` (pinning direct edges without requiring transitive-only dependencies such as `clj` via `clojure.core` to be duplicated at the root).\n   300\t     - Recursively walks every `:requires` edge starting from `:yang.prelude/root-address` across `artifact-store`, verifying that every transitively reachable manifest address and `:yin.module/tree` address resolves, that the full transitive `:requires` DAG is finite and acyclic, and that no two distinct addresses bind the same linker module symbol anywhere in the closure.\n65:   - Composition facts (which `yrt.*` modules a prelude requires) live in the explicit module `:requires` DAG, never as a redundant tag in UAST rows.\n78:6. **No assumed graphs:** Every composed prelude declares an explicit, acyclic `:requires` DAG over an **immutable, verified artifact closure**. Missing exports, missing transitive artifacts, or cycles fail closed at validation\n81:   - **`yrt.*` modules, `clj.py`, and Layer-2c standard libraries (`clojure.core.impl`, `clojure.core`) MUST NEVER declare (`:yin.module/primitives`) or export (`:yin.module/exports`) provenance-door primitives directly.** (Not\n103:                                      | composes explicitly via :requires DAG\n123:| **Module / import loaders** | Python `sys.modules` + package hierarchy, JS ESM link/eval stacks + live bindings, and PHP dynamic `include`/`require` scope-cell adoption have incompatible lifecycle rules. |\n147:    - `kind`: `:finally`, `:handler`, `:generator`, or any language-installed non-`:finally` boundary tag.\n154:  - Both `py/gen-start` (`yang.python.antlr.prelude:471`) and `php/gen-start` (`yang.php.antlr.prelude:5312`) install `:generator` frames whose payload is `(fn [e] (gen-fail g e))`.\n185:Used by: `py`, `js`, `php`, `clj.py`, standalone `clojure.core` (omitted by default `clj`). Host dependencies (P1): `data/float64`, `data/float-value`, `data/content=`, `data/count`, `data/nth`, `data/str-concat`, `integer/shi\n206:| `fmod-pos` | **Leaf raw; requires finite `x >= 0` and finite `y > 0`** (callers exclude NaN, `±Inf`, `y = 0`, negative signs beforehand) | Pure Sterbenz long-division remainder loop; returns unwrapped double inside caller l\n207:| `fpow-half-raw`, `fpow-base-raw` | **Leaf raw; requires unwrapped `base`, exact integer `e >= 0`** | Integer-exponent squaring (`py`/`js` order vs. `php` order); zero callbacks |\n245:   Used by `yang.core.prelude` + `yang.core.prelude-admission` to produce the module's UAST, schema-1 manifest, and C1 side table from the owning language's definition list, with direct pins, executable trailing `require` form\n257:    {:cell {:required true}\n258:     :data {:required true, :min-max-items 1048576}\n259:     :integer {:required true, :min-bits 53}}\n265:     :trailing-requires []         ;; explicit trailing `(require '<mod>)` vector: `[]` for standardized base preludes (`py`/`js`/`php`/`clj`/`yang.call`), `['py]`/`['js]` only for safepoint overlays (`py.sp`/`js.sp`)\n285:    {:cell {:required true}\n286:     :data {:required true, :min-max-items 1048576}\n287:     :integer {:required true, :min-bits 53}}\n288:    :yang.prelude/max-effects nil} ;; optional allowed-effect ceiling: for standardized linked `py` (`:trailing-requires []`), the verified footprint is `#{:cell/new :cell/get :cell/set! :cell/authentic? :cell/new-provenance :\n299:     - Every `[sym addr]` in `:yang.prelude/components` and `:yang.prelude/root-address` resolves in `artifact-store`, and the root manifest's direct `:requires` map matches `:yang.prelude/components` (pinning direct edges wit\n300:     - Recursively walks every `:requires` edge starting from `:yang.prelude/root-address` across `artifact-store`, verifying that every transitively reachable manifest address and `:yin.module/tree` address resolves, that the\n308:   - Rather than duplicating the manifest's derived effect set (honoring \"Derive, don't persist\"), `:yang.prelude/max-effects` is strictly optional. When present, admission checks `(clojure.set/subset? derived-transitive-effec\n311:   - Verifies that `registry` supplies every required host export (`prelude-admission/admit`) AND verifies every declared floor in `:yang.prelude/host-modules` (`:min-bits`, `:min-digits`, `:min-max-items`) against the trusted\n313:   - **Standardized linked emission (`P0` clean-slate normalization):** derives `:requires` and `:skip?` directly from `:yang.prelude/components`; emits trailing `require` forms **only** from explicit `:trailing-requires` (`[]\n338:  1. Its **fixed Hook ABI table** (`{hook-key {:arity n :required-by [...]}}`) specifying exact parameter conventions and structural lowering shapes for that frontend's grammar.\n377:  :control/exceptions   :supported     ;; bare `except:` + `finally` + `raise` (`except Exc as e:` requires :control/except-typed; `except as e:` is invalid Python 3 grammar)\n488:     - Computes the descriptor's **selected, address-verified closure**: every `[module address]` in `:yang.semantics/ambient-modules` must resolve in `artifact-store` (both its verified manifest AND its `:yin.module/tree` can\n491:       - **Hooks and executable `:literals.*` targets:** verifies the symbol is namespace-qualified, exists in `:yin.module/exports` of `m` in the **selected, address-verified closure** (or an authorized host module in `regist\n515:No `yang.frontend` schema change is required (`src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc`):\n516:- `:yang.frontend/id` continues to name the frontend syntax + lowering implementation (e.g., `:yang.python/antlr`), and each distinct configuration receives a distinct immutable `:yang.frontend/revision` (e.g., `\"py-v1\"` vs. `\n598:   - **Why a uniform key/element gate is required (`yin/vm/data.cljc:34–36`, `dao.jing.cbor.md:173, 266`):** Host map/set hashing and Jing canonical CBOR encoding cannot recover distinct keys once collapsed by host collectio\n664:   - Given metadata map `meta` and binder/executor thunk `bind-and-run`, allocates the owner cell **first**, installs `entry` closing over that initialized `owner` binding via `cell/set!`, and returns `owner` (mirroring the wo\n736:   - Requires **`clj`** and **`clojure.core.impl`**. Exports ONLY cell-free pure functions at install time (`src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:915, 1055`):\n744:   - Adding `'clojure.core` to `:requires` exposes nothing to user code on its own; only explicit entries in `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` enter source scope.\n795:- Whenever prelude normalization (`P0` uniform `:trailing-requires` / `:finalize-c1?`), runtime extraction (`P1` `yrt.*`), uniform Hook ABI signatures (`P2` 2-arg `:unit/run-main`), or Clojure stdlib unification (`P3`) changes\n803:| **P0 — Uniform composition plumbing & `defquoted` consolidation** | Consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.prelude`; implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` (with independent `:components`, explicit `:trailing-requires`, uniform\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
