(= response-stream :php/null))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '140,182p;600,616p;628,637p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc | sed -n '156,204p'\nrg -n 'defn.*(preamble|unshadow|hygien)|dsg__get|kernel-alias|primitive-names' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '140,182p;600,616p;628,637p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc | sed -n '156,204p'\nrg -n 'defn.*(preamble|unshadow|hygien)|dsg__get|kernel-alias|primitive-names' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   140\tUsed by: `py`, `js`, `php`, `clj`, `clj.py`. Host dependencies: `cell/get`, `cell/set!`, `cell/new`, `data/nth`.\n   141\t\n   142\tReconciles the current per-language divergences (`4-slot` vs `5-slot` frames, `:base` rebasing, `:generator` boundary frames, `orelse` vs value-return, PHP `abandon-to`, normal-exit `finally` sentinel, and empty-stack handling) by parameterizing `ctx-cell`, `normal-arg`, and `on-empty`:\n   143\t\n   144\t- **Unified context record:** `{:handlers hs :depth d :base b :frame f}`.\n   145\t  - **4-to-5-slot migration for `js` and `clj`:** Currently `yang.typescript.antlr.prelude` and `yang.clojure.prelude` allocate `{:handlers hs}` and push 4-slot frames `[tag payload rest n]`. In P1, `js/init!`, `clj/init!`, and bundled `yang.clojure` migrate to `(yrt.escape/ctx nil 0 0 nil)` and 5-slot frames.\n   146\t  - **Distinct slot meanings (`n` vs. `depth`):** In the 5-slot frame `[kind payload rest n depth]`:\n   147\t    - `kind`: `:finally`, `:handler`, `:generator`, or any language-installed non-`:finally` boundary tag.\n   148\t    - `payload`: continuation `r` (for `:handler` / `:generator` boundary dispatch) or cleanup closure `fin` (for `:finally`).\n   149\t    - `rest`: enclosing frame (or `nil`).\n   150\t    - **`n` (slot 3):** monotonic handler-stack frame count `(+ 1 (frame-depth rest))` used strictly by `unwind-to` and `abandon-to` for O(1) structural depth comparison (`<= (data/nth hs 3) n`).\n   151\t    - **`depth` (slot 4):** activation-relative function call depth at the moment the frame was pushed, restored onto `:depth` by `pop-frame` (`py` and `php` recursion/safepoint accounting). Languages without call-depth hooks (`js`, `clj`) keep `depth = 0`.\n   152\t- **Capture-safe vector frame reads (`data/nth`):** Every read of the 5-slot frame vector (`kind`, `payload`, `rest`, `n`, `depth`) inside `yrt.escape` uses **`data/nth`** (`(data/nth hs 0)` … `(data/nth hs 4)`), reserving `get` strictly for the context-map fields (`:handlers`, `:depth`, `:base`). Because `data/nth` is a qualified host module export, source-defined `(defn get ...)` can never corrupt frame dispatch or stack traversal.\n   153\t- **Open boundary-frame dispatch (preserving generators in P1):**\n   154\t  - Both `py/gen-start` (`yang.python.antlr.prelude:471`) and `php/gen-start` (`yang.php.antlr.prelude:5312`) install `:generator` frames whose payload is `(fn [e] (gen-fail g e))`.\n   155\t  - Accordingly, `yrt.escape/raise` MUST dispatch `(if (= (data/nth hs 0) :finally) ... ((data/nth hs 1) e))` — treating `:finally` specially and delivering `e` to `(data/nth hs 1)` for **every non-`:finally` frame kind** (`:handler`, `:generator`, etc.), never restricting allowed kinds to a closed two-kind check! Existing generators remain 100% compatible during P1 even before `yrt.gen` is extracted in P4.\n   156\t- **`restore!` invariant:** `(fn [ctx-cell saved] (cell/set! ctx-cell (assoc saved :base (get (cell/get ctx-cell) :base))))` — always preserves the activation's current `:base` across generator crossings.\n   157\t\n   158\t**Public exports:**\n   159\t\n   160\t| Export | Signature | Behavior |\n   161\t|---|---|---|\n   162\t| `ctx` | `[handlers depth base frame]` | Construct context record |\n   163\t| `handlers` / `set-handlers!` / `restore!` | `[ctx-cell ...]` | Context cell accessors/mutators (`restore!` preserves live `:base`) |\n   164\t| `frame-depth` / `frame` / `pop-frame` | `[hs]` / `[ctx-cell kind payload rest]` / `[ctx-cell hs]` | Frame construction and unwind pop (restoring `:handlers` and `:depth` via `data/nth`) |\n   165\t| `raise` | `[ctx-cell e on-empty]` | Pop & invoke `:finally` frames passing `e`; invoke `(data/nth hs 1)` on any non-`:finally` frame; call `(on-empty e)` if stack is empty (`py`/`js`/`clj` return a sentinel; `php` triggers `invariant-violation`) |\n   166\t| `unwind-to` | `[ctx-cell n normal-arg]` | Pop frames while `(> (data/nth hs 3) n)`, running each `:finally` thunk with `normal-arg` (`:py/None`, `:js/undefined`, `:php/null`, `nil`) |\n   167\t| `abandon-to` | `[ctx-cell n]` | Pop frames while `(> (data/nth hs 3) n)` **without** running `:finally` thunks (PHP terminal fatals / `exit`) |\n   168\t| `try-orelse` | `[ctx-cell body handler orelse]` | Install `:handler`; on normal exit restore and tail-call `(orelse)`; on escape restore and call `(handler r)` (`py`, `php`, and Python `try/except/else` in `clj.py`) |\n   169\t| `try-value` | `[ctx-cell body handler]` | Install `:handler`; on normal exit restore and return `(body)`'s value directly (`js`, `clj`, and `clj.py` / `clojure.core` function entry boundaries) |\n   170\t| `try-finally` | `[ctx-cell body fin normal-arg]` | Install `:finally`; on normal exit restore, run `(fin normal-arg)`, return `v` |\n   171\t| `call-ec` | `[ctx-cell f normal-arg]` | Capture escape continuation that runs `unwind-to` then `restore!` before invoking `r` |\n   172\t| `call-terminal` | `[ctx-cell f]` | Capture terminal escape that runs `abandon-to` then `restore!` before invoking `r` (`php`) |\n   173\t\n   174\t**Capture-safety for bundled `yang.clojure`:**\n   175\t- In `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2470–2517`, the live preamble currently constructs **four** portable guest helpers (`dsg__get`, `dsg__equal`, `dsg__assoc`, `dsg__empty`), while `conj` and `vec` are protected against local shadowing by the convention's binder checks (`clojure.cljc:2479`), and `+` / `<=` currently have no `dsg__*` helpers. Note that `dsg__get` (`clojure.cljc:2484–2497`) scans only maps (`data/map?`) and returns `nil` on vectors.\n   176\t- Because `yrt.escape` accesses all vector frames via `data/nth`, bundled `yrt.escape/uast` needs `get` only for context maps (`:handlers`, `:depth`, `:base`). Even so, as defense-in-depth, extending `dsg__get` (or keeping a dedicated guest helper) to handle non-negative integer indexing on `data/vector?` via `data/nth` ensures no bundled frame/context lookup can ever return `nil` when source code defines `(defn get ...)`.\n   177\t- Thus, when `yrt.escape/uast` is bundled inline into non-linked `yang.clojure`, it reads `get`, `=`, `assoc`, `conj`, `+`, and `<=` as follows without breaking UCF machine-data validation (never binding host primitive functions inside guest environments):\n   178\t  - `[get = assoc]` bind to the existing portable guest closures `[dsg__get dsg__equal dsg__assoc]` (with `dsg__get` supporting both maps and vectors, and `yrt.escape` reading frames via `data/nth`);\n   179\t  - `conj` continues to rely on `yang.clojure`'s binder-check refusal;\n   180\t  - `+` and `<=` are wrapped by adding two portable guest closures `dsg__add` and `dsg__lte` (using `(+ a b)` / `(<= a b)` when unshadowed, and safe binary integer arithmetic or binder-check refusal when `+` or `<=` is defined in `(::defined env)` — all pure guest lambdas, matching `dsg__get` at `clojure.cljc:2484`).\n   181\t- In linked mode, module lexical isolation makes the `dsg__*` wrapper unnecessary.\n   182\t\n   600\t     - **Admitted keys / set elements (recursively):**\n   601\t       - `nil`, booleans, exact integers (`integer/integer?`), strings;\n   602\t       - **Unambiguous keywords (`kind/keyword?`) and symbols (`kind/symbol?`):** letting `ns = (kind/namespace k)` and `nm = (kind/name k)`, `admit-key!` refuses with `{:clj.py/error :unsupported-key :key k}` whenever `ns` is empty (`\"\"`), `ns` contains `\"/\"` (`(not (nil? (data/str-index-of ns \"/\")))`), `nm` contains `\"/\"` (refusing `(keyword nil \"a/b\")` / `(symbol nil \"a/b\")` cleanly on EVERY host!), or `nm` begins with `\":\"` (`(if (> (data/str-length nm) 0) (= (data/substring nm 0 1) \":\") false)`). Because `(kind, ns, nm) -> joined-name` is strictly injective on admitted identifiers, CLJS joined-name map/set collapse (`dao.jing.cbor.md:266`) cannot happen;\n   603\t       - Persistent vectors, persistent maps (both keys and values checked recursively), and persistent sets recursively containing **only** admitted values.\n   604\t     - **Refused keys / set elements at ANY nesting depth:** any `data/float64?` value (`0.0`, `-0.0`, `1.0`, `NaN`, `±Inf`, or nested `[[-0.0]]`, `{\"a\" 1.0}`), ambiguous identifiers (`(keyword nil \"a/b\")`, `(symbol nil \"a/b\")`, `[(keyword nil \"a/b\")]`), lists/seqs (`seq?`, preventing list-vs-vector collisions), host closures/continuations, and `:cell-ref` handles — raising guest error `{:clj.py/error :unsupported-key :key k}` (`ex-info` in `clojure.core.impl`).\n   605\t     - Arbitrary floats (`-0.0`, `1.0`, `NaN`, `±Inf`), arbitrary identifiers (`(keyword nil \"a/b\")`), lists, and callables remain **fully supported as scalar values, map values, and vector/list elements**!\n   606\t   - **Recursive portable equality (`clj.py/eq`, `clj.py/ne` and `clojure.core.impl/impl-not=`):** Never delegates floats, float-bearing collections, or identifiers (keywords/symbols) to host `=`, because CLJS `Float64.-equiv` (`src/cljc/dao/host/number.cljc:98–101`) equates `NaN` with `NaN` and distinguishes `-0.0` from `0.0`, and CLJS identifier `=` equates `(keyword nil \"a/b\")` with `(keyword \"a\" \"b\")` (`dao.jing.cbor.md:266`):\n   607\t     - `:int` × `:int`: `(= (integer/compare a b) 0)`.\n   608\t     - `:float` × `:float`: leaf unwrap → `false` if either is NaN, else `(= ax bx)` (`+0.0 == -0.0` is `true`, `NaN == NaN` is `false` on all 4 hosts).\n   609\t     - `:int` × `:float` (or vice versa): **`false`** (`1 != 1.0`).\n   610\t     - Identifiers (`kind/keyword?`, `kind/symbol?`): compared strictly by kind + nullable namespace (`cmp-opt-str == 0`) + name (`(data/str-compare (kind/name a) (kind/name b)) == 0`), so `(keyword nil \"a/b\") == (keyword \"a\" \"b\")` is **`false`** on all 4 hosts including CLJS/Node.\n   611\t     - Vectors / sequential collections (`data/vector?`, `clojure.core.impl/impl-sequential?`): equal count + pairwise recursive `eq`.\n   612\t     - Maps (`data/map?`, excluding authenticated `:cell-ref` handles): equal count + every admitted key `k` present in both with values recursively equal via `eq` — so `{\"a\": -0.0} == {\"a\": 0.0}` is `true` and `{\"a\": NaN} == {\"a\": NaN}` is `false` on all 4 hosts.\n   613\t     - Sets (`kind/set?`): equal count + exact admitted membership across all elements.\n   614\t     - Other scalars (`nil`, booleans, strings, authenticated `:cell-ref` handles): host `=`.\n   615\t\n   616\t### 7.3 Python lowering Hook ABI & `clj.py` adapters\n   628\t| `:ctrl/try-finally` | `[body fin]` | Calls `yrt.escape/try-finally` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` with `normal-arg = nil`. |\n   629\t| `:ctrl/raise` | `[e]` | Calls `clj/raise` (delegating to `yrt.escape/raise` on `(clj/rt-ctx)`). |\n   630\t| `:ctrl/call-ec` | `[f]` | Calls `yrt.escape/call-ec` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` with `normal-arg = nil`. |\n   631\t| `:ctrl/for-each` | `[iterable step-fn]` | Invokes collision-free implementation entries **`clojure.core.impl/impl-seq`**, **`impl-first`**, and **`impl-rest`** directly (zero collision with 0-arg public `clojure.core` export accessors!), iterates deterministic canonical `[k v]` pairs for maps and canonical elements for sets, raises guest error on non-collection iterables, and invokes `step-fn` per element (supports `break`/`continue` via `call-ec` and eager comprehensions). |\n   632\t| `:comp/list-new`, `:comp/set-new`, `:comp/dict-new` | `[init-vec]`, `[]`, `[]` | Allocates a temporary local accumulator cell holding persistent `[]`, `#{}`, or `{}` (`cell/new []`, `cell/new #{}`, `cell/new {}`). |\n   633\t| `:comp/list-append`, `:comp/set-add`, `:comp/dict-set` | `[acc val]`, `[acc val]`, `[acc k v]` | Reads `(cell/get acc)`, validates set elements / dict keys via `admit-key!`, updates via `(cell/set! acc (conj cur val))` / `(assoc cur k v)`, and returns `:py/None` (in `clj.py`, `nil`). |\n   634\t| `:comp/finish` | `[acc]` *(optional)* | Returns `(cell/get acc)` (the immutable persistent vector/set/map). Omitted (`nil`) in `:yang.python/py-v1` so mutable-accumulator Python lowering keeps zero overhead. |\n   635\t| `:unit/run-main` | `[body-fn ambient-resolver]` | Calls idempotent `(clj/init!)`, `(clojure.core/init!)`, and `(clj.py/init!)` (where `clj.py` exports idempotent 0-arg `init!`, 1-arg `export` via `clj/prim-get`, and 0-arg cell-accessor `ex-info`, satisfying `§6.4`'s `:cell-accessor` contract); allocates a **fresh per-unit `globals` cell** `(cell/new (assoc (assoc {} :vars {}) :ambient ambient-resolver))` and `globals-fn`; invokes `(body-fn globals globals-fn)` inside a top-level handler on `(clj/rt-ctx)`; returns the value **verbatim without stripping `[:yin.k/ok ...]`** so ordinary Python data shaped like `[:yin.k/ok 42]` passes through uncorrupted. |\n   636\t\n   637\t*(Lowerings with `:mutation/locals :single-assignment` remain a separate, stricter profile variant that omits local variable cells and refuses assignment/reassignment to locals, loops with mutated accumulators, and `nonlocal`.)*\n   156\t    ;; ------------------------------------------------------------- entry\n   157\t    ;; The outcome model's `[:yin.k/ok value]` wrapper is frontend-\n   158\t    ;; internal, so the entry removes one wrapper level from the\n   159\t    ;; program's value (a program returning that vector as data was\n   160\t    ;; wrapped again, so one level is exact). An error outcome passes\n   161\t    ;; through as the failure value for the caller to render.\n   162\t    [clj/unwrap-outcome\n   163\t     (fn [value]\n   164\t       (if (if (data/vector? value) (= (data/count value) 2) false)\n   165\t         (if (= (data/nth value 0) :yin.k/ok)\n   166\t           (data/nth value 1)\n   167\t           value)\n   168\t         value))]\n   169\t    ;; The global namespace is the task's, not the entry's: no reset\n   170\t    ;; here, so projections and earlier units' definitions survive.\n   171\t    [clj/run-main\n   172\t     (fn [body]\n   173\t       (do (clj/init!)\n   174\t           (clj/unwrap-outcome (body))))]])\n   175\t\n   176\t\n   177\t(def module-definitions\n   178\t  \"The module's definition list: an `:clj/uninit` placeholder for every\n   179\t   runtime key, then every definition, stripped.\"\n   180\t  (core/module-definitions \"clj\" :clj/uninit runtime-keys definitions))\n   181\t\n   182\t\n   183\t(def module-uast\n   184\t  \"The module tree: one wide application over the definitions, so every\n   185\t   sibling and runtime key read is discharged at module level. C1\n   186\t   finalized, like every production `yang.clojure` tree.\"\n   187\t  (yang/annotate-call-sites (core/module-tree module-definitions [])))\n   188\t\n   189\t\n   190\t(def module-exports\n   191\t  \"The module's exports: every `clj/` key of the definition list, stripped.\"\n   192\t  (core/exports \"clj\" definitions))\n   193\t\n   194\t\n   195\t(def ^:private module-free-names\n   196\t  \"The names the module tree reads and does not define, sorted: the host\n   197\t   exports its manifest must declare.\"\n   198\t  (core/free-name-vec module-uast))\n   199\t\n   200\t\n   201\t(defn module-spec\n   202\t  \"`yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!`'s spec for the module `clj` over\n   203\t   the host registry `registry`, pinned to the published `yang.call`\n   204\t   module at `call-address` — the convention's call-address, as every\n944:    [clj/handlers (fn [] (dsg__get (cell/get clj.rt/ctx) :handlers))]\n949:    [clj/frame-depth (fn [hs] (if (dsg__equal hs nil) 0 (dsg__get hs 3)))]\n957:                  (dsg__assoc (cell/get clj.rt/ctx) :handlers (dsg__get hs 2))))]\n962:           (dsg__get e :clj/no-handler)\n963:           (if (dsg__equal (dsg__get hs 0) :finally)\n964:             (do (clj/pop-frame hs) ((dsg__get hs 1) e) (clj/raise e))\n965:             ((dsg__get hs 1) e)))))]\n974:                  (clj/set-handlers! (clj/frame :handler r (dsg__get saved :handlers)))\n981:         (do (clj/set-handlers! (clj/frame :finally fin (dsg__get saved :handlers)))\n987:  '(fn [dsg__value] (dsg__get dsg__value :yin.k/message)))\n991:  '(fn [dsg__value] (dsg__get dsg__value :yin.k/data)))\n1226:        positional (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/positional))\n1227:        named (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/named))\n1228:        raise (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/raise))\n1404:  (let [seal (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) callee (u/lit :seal))]\n1406:                      (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) callee (u/lit :type))\n1443:                                                   (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v condition)\n1446:                                            (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v condition)\n2376:                                                  (dsg__get dsg__candidate :type)\n2386:                                                          (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n2390:                                                              (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n2405:                                                  (dsg__get dsg__descriptor\n2410:                                                (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n2413:                                                (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n2434:                                                           'dsg__get\n2452:                                      (dsg__get dsg__descriptor :yang.call/entry)\n2473:                                      (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n2483:                               (u/lam '[dsg__get dsg__equal dsg__assoc dsg__empty] %)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
