{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '646,695p' docs/design/yang.preludes.md\nsed -n '25,54p' src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc\nsed -n '178,231p' docs/design/yang.preludes.md | tail -22\nrg -n 'nth|normalize|small.*big|bigint.*key|content-key' docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md | head -24\nrg --files --hidden -g '*cljs*.js' -g '*cljs*.mjs' | head -20\nrg -n 'D[оo]or|expos|raw.*source|primitives' docs/design/yang.preludes.md | cut -c1-180 | tail -18\"","aggregated_output":"`clj` enforces the full §8.10 + §8.10.7 contract:\n\n1. **Source-level callable admission (`clj/admitted-callable?`):**\n   - Called by `clj/invoke-callable`, `clj.py/callable?`, `clojure.core.impl/impl-fn?`, and `clojure.core.impl`'s dynamic higher-order caller **before** invoking `yang.call/invoke`. Written strictly in prelude special-form notation (`src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc:82` — nested `if`, zero `and` form!):\n     ```clojure\n     (if (data/map? x)\n       (if (= (get x :type) :cell-ref)\n         (if (cell/authentic? x)\n           (if (data/callable? (yang.call/entry x))\n             (yang.call/eligible? x)\n             false)\n           false)\n         false)\n       false)\n     ```\n   - Any plain source map (including `{:yang.call/entry ...}`), unauthenticated `{:type :cell-ref ...}` map, or raw host primitive/continuation fails `admitted-callable?` cleanly; `invoke-callable` mints a retained `:yang.call/not-callable` protocol condition via private `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and raises it via `(clj/raise ...)`, never calling `yang.call/invoke` on forged source data.\n   - Preserves zero-wrapper function identity (`=`) across all cell-backed frontends (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core`).\n2. **Two-step cell-backed callable constructor (`clj/make-callable`):**\n   - Given metadata map `meta` and binder/executor thunk `bind-and-run`, allocates the owner cell **first**, installs `entry` closing over that initialized `owner` binding via `cell/set!`, and returns `owner` (mirroring the working two-step pattern at `src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:944–960`):\n     ```clojure\n     (let [owner (cell/new meta)\n           entry (fn [invocation] ...)] ;; closes over `owner` & enforces Step 3\n       (do (cell/set! owner (assoc meta :yang.call/entry entry))\n           owner))\n     ```\n3. **Full 4-step invocation-record validation & §8.10.7 entry boundary (with evaluated `assoc` condition evidence):**\n   - **Step A — Establish usable raise exit first:** verify `(data/map? invocation)` and `(data/callable? (get invocation :yang.call/raise))`. If missing or non-callable, fail operationally right away (never invoke an invalid exit or convert wiring corruption into a guest catchable error).\n   - **Step B — Validate protocol record & owner identity (outside `try-value`):** check `(yang.call/valid-invocation? invocation)` AND `(= (get invocation :yang.call/callee) owner)`. Because `yang.core.uast/sexp->uast` emits map literals unevaluated (`src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc:82`), build the condition evidence via **evaluated `assoc` calls** before transferring:\n     ```clojure\n     (yang.call/transfer\n       raise-exit\n       (yang.call/condition :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n                            (assoc {} :yang.call/callee owner)))\n     ```\n   - **Step C — Reject unsupported binding extensions (outside `try-value`):** if `(data/contains? invocation :yang.call/binding-profile)`, build evidence with **evaluated `assoc` calls** and transfer:\n     ```clojure\n     (yang.call/transfer\n       raise-exit\n       (yang.call/condition\n         :yang.call/unsupported-binding\n         (assoc (assoc {} :yang.call/callee owner)\n                :yang.call/binding-profile (get invocation :yang.call/binding-profile))))\n     ```\n   - **Step D — Value-returning boundary (`yrt.escape/try-value` — NOT `try-orelse`!) around binding + body:**\n     - Installs the exception handler on `(clj/rt-ctx)` **before** argument binding so ordinary named-arg / positional-arity errors share the same boundary: inside `try-value`, `(bind-and-run positional named)` checks `:yang.call/named` and positional/varargs arity against `:spec` (raising local guest binding exceptions via `clj/raise` so they cross under **`:yang.call/thrown`**) and evaluates the body.\n     - On normal completion, `yrt.escape/try-value` restores `(clj/rt-ctx)` and returns the body's value verbatim (`20` in §7.6).\n     - On escape with `e`, the handler inspects private `(cell/dsg__provenance e)`: if non-nil (an authentic retained protocol condition from a deeper cross-language boundary), forwards that retained condition **directly** to `raise-exit` without double-wrapping; otherwise wraps `e` (including condition-shaped user maps!) via `(yang.call/thrown e)` and transfers it to `raise-exit`.\n4. **Call-site boundary (`clj/invoke-callable`):**\n   - Validates `(clj/admitted-callable? callee)`; if false, mints private retained `:yang.call/not-callable` via `cell/dsg__new-provenance` (with evaluated `(assoc {} :yang.call/callee callee)` evidence) and raises on `(clj/rt-ctx)`.\n   - Otherwise calls `yang.call/invoke` with a dedicated `raise-exit` closure:\n    ;; dereferenced only when the heap authenticates it (`cell/authentic?`,\n    ;; the issuer's own answer). A map that imitates the reference language\n    ;; is data, so it projects to itself and its fate follows the ordinary\n    ;; descriptor rules, exactly as any other map's would.\n    [yang.call/_descriptor\n     (fn [callable]\n       (if (data/map? callable)\n         (if (if (= (get callable :type) :cell-ref)\n               (cell/authentic? callable)\n               false)\n           (cell/get callable)\n           callable)\n         nil))]\n    [yang.call/entry\n     (fn [callable]\n       (get (yang.call/_descriptor callable) :yang.call/entry))]\n    [yang.call/eligible?\n     (fn [callable]\n       (let [descriptor (yang.call/_descriptor callable)]\n         (if (nil? (yang.call/entry callable))\n           false\n           (if (data/contains? descriptor :yang.call/eligible?)\n             ((get descriptor :yang.call/eligible?) callable)\n             true))))]\n    [yang.call/invocation\n     (fn [callee positional named raise]\n       (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :yang.call/callee callee)\n                            :yang.call/positional positional)\n                     :yang.call/named named)\n              :yang.call/raise raise))]\n| `float-floor-raw`, `float-floor` | `float-floor-raw [x]` (leaf raw); `float-floor [x-boxed]` (boxed) | Total IEEE double floor: binary descent + `data/float-value` for finite `|x| < 2^53`, returning `x` unchanged for `|x| >= 2^53`, `±Inf`, `NaN`; zero callbacks |\n| `float-parts` | **Requires finite nonzero unwrapped `x`** (caller excludes `0.0`, `NaN`, `±Inf` beforehand) | Returns exact `[mantissa exp2]` integer pair (safe integer tuple; no raw double returned) |\n| `zeros`, `exp-text` | Exact counts/exponents | Pure string layout helpers over `integer/float-digits` |\n\n### 4.4 `yrt.int` — exact-integer helpers and fixed-width wrapping\n\nUsed by: `py`, `js`, `php`, `clj.py` (omitted by `clj`). Host dependencies: `data/count`, `data/nth`, `integer/*`.\n\n**`yin.vm.integer` v4 refusal algebra (`src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc:81–100`):**\n- `yin.vm.integer` v4 **returns** keyword reasons in place of a result for exactly **three** resource/range conditions: `:yin.vm.integer/bit-limit`, `:yin.vm.integer/digit-limit`, and `:yin.vm.integer/float-overflow`.\n- Every other refusal (`:arity`, `:wrong-type`, `:out-of-range`, `:syntax`, `:zero-division`, `:negative-count`, `:negative-exponent`) **throws** a host operational failure indicating a caller-side defect (`integer.cljc:93–100`) and **MUST NOT** be caught or relabeled into guest exceptions.\n\n**Public exports:**\n- **`check-limit`** (`[res on-bit-limit on-digit-limit on-float-overflow]`): inspects `res` strictly against the three returned keywords (`:yin.vm.integer/bit-limit`, `:yin.vm.integer/digit-limit`, `:yin.vm.integer/float-overflow`), invoking the matching policy closure and returning `res` unchanged for every valid integer, float, boolean, string, or `[q r]` pair.\n  - *(Language-specific adapter ownership:)* `php/int-result` (`yang.php.antlr.prelude:902`) performs signed-64-bit demotion to float (`(if (php/in-range? n) n (php/f (integer/to-float n)))`) rather than Python/JS's exception mapping; PHP therefore keeps `php/int-result` in Layer 2b built over `yrt.int/in-range?` and `yrt.int/check-limit`.\n- **Fixed-width wrapping:** `wrap-unsigned` (`[x width-pow2 mask]`) and `wrap-signed` (`[x half-range range]`), backing `js/wrap32` / `js/to-int32` / `js/to-uint32` and `php/wrap64`; `in-range?` (`[x min-v max-v]`).\n- **Generic digit & scanner primitives:** `digit-value` (`[code-point]`), `all-digits?` (`[cs i n radix]`), `scan-digits` (`[cs i n radix acc]`), `skip-while` (`[cs i n pred?]`), `skip-zeros` (`[cs i n]`). Each language supplies its own whitespace predicate (`pred?`), sign, prefix, and underscore syntax rules in Layer 2b.\n- **Admission ownership:** Per-language integer floors (`min-integer-bits = 53` for `py`/`js`/`clj.py`; `min-integer-bits = 4096, min-integer-digits = 1000` for `php`) stay enforced by each language profile's admission check, not hardcoded inside `yrt.int`.\n\n### 4.5 `yrt.gen` and `yrt.safepoint` *(Tier-2 shared components, Slice P4)*\n\nDeferred to Slice P4 (after core + math lands) to bound P1 migration scope:\n283:addresses. Host integer width is not identity; small and big integers of the\n338:example a content-key-ordered structure), a real interface change the\n66:4. **Everything is a Continuation:** Shared control-flow primitives (`yrt.escape`) and coroutine stepping (`yrt.gen`) remain pure guest UAST over `%capture` and task-heap cells \n81:   - **`yrt.*` modules, `clj.py`, and Layer-2c standard libraries (`clojure.core.impl`, `clojure.core`) MUST NEVER declare (`:yin.module/primitives`) or export (`:yin.module/exp\n82:   - **No descriptor hook or source-facing ambient projection** may expose `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, `yang.safepoint/*`, or non-projectable internal\n83:   - Retained protocol-condition provenance (`yang.antlr.md` §8.10.7) resides strictly inside trusted Layer-2b runtime modules (`py`, `js`, `php`, **`clj`**) in **both** bundle\n110:                                      | host-declared pure/effect primitives\n226:- **Generic digit & scanner primitives:** `digit-value` (`[code-point]`), `all-digits?` (`[cs i n radix]`), `scan-digits` (`[cs i n radix acc]`), `skip-while` (`[cs i n pred?]`\n267:     :capture-safe-primitives nil} ;; optional for bundled clj mode\n306:   - Therefore, validation enforces the provenance-door exclusion against each non-trusted module's (`yrt.*`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core.impl`, `clojure.core`) **direct** `:yin.mo\n491:       - **Hooks and executable `:literals.*` targets:** verifies the symbol is namespace-qualified, exists in `:yin.module/exports` of `m` in the **selected, address-verified \n495:     - **Reserved-door ban:** Refuses any descriptor whose `:hooks`, executable `:literals.*` fields, or `:ambient-projections` references `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `\n661:   - Any plain source map (including `{:yang.call/entry ...}`), unauthenticated `{:type :cell-ref ...}` map, or raw host primitive/continuation fails `admitted-callable?` clean\n701:In Slice P3, the portable Clojure standard library is split cleanly into two complementary Layer-2c linker modules — eliminating **all** store-key collisions against VM primi\n744:   - Adding `'clojure.core` to `:requires` exposes nothing to user code on its own; only explicit entries in `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` enter source scope.\n790:- **Bounded public APIs:** Host namespaces maintain 2–5 `defn` entry points (`yang.core.semantics`: `valid