{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-20 18:31:51 GMT  \nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-20 13:31:51 EST (-0500)\n\n## 1. Verdict\n\n**`REVISE` — 7 of 9 r4 findings are `CONFIRMED-FIXED`.** The unified `clj` ownership, linked `clojure.core` facade, two-step callable constructor, and per-unit ambient resolver resolve their original defects. Two findings remain open. The identifier gate calls a string primitive on an absent namespace, and descriptor admission still lacks sufficient evidence for some executable targets.\n\nThe clean-slate direction stands. The most consequential new gaps concern behavior the unified runtime must carry forward: PHP’s request and output streams, native Clojure collection invocation, and bundled Clojure execution when source code shadows a primitive.\n\nI reviewed the 831-line working-tree design at `9cf135c2`, the prior findings, and the referenced implementation and specification contracts. This was a read-only design review. **No files were edited.** The four-host, language-oracle, and repository suites were not run.\n\n## 2. r4 finding-by-finding disposition\n\nDesign line numbers refer to [docs/design/yang.preludes.md](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md).\n\n| r4 | Disposition | Design and live-code evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| #1 Provenance ownership and transitive footprints | `CONFIRMED-FIXED` | Lines 80–83, 304–308, 641–643, and 745 put both emitters’ private doors in `clj`, check consumers’ direct declarations, and apply the ceiling to the transitive footprint. This matches publication’s dependency-effect union. [Footprint derivation](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:81) |\n| #2 Linked facade shadows primitive names | `CONFIRMED-FIXED` | Lines 644, 703–706, and 735–740 give the implementation `impl-*` store keys and route facade lookup and insertion through `clj/prim-get` and `clj/prim-assoc`. This resolves the reported linked recursion under namespace stripping and store-first lookup. Bundled execution has a separate issue below. [Module definitions](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc:42) · [VM lookup](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:116) |\n| #3 Callable owner and evaluated evidence | `CONFIRMED-FIXED` | Lines 663–694 allocate the owner before installing its entry, build condition evidence with evaluated `assoc`, and put binding and execution inside `try-value`. The P3 gate checks the actual owner and binding profile at the raise exit. [Working Python constructor](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:944) · [UAST emission](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc:88) |\n| #4 Portable identifiers in keys and equality | `OPEN` | Lines 602, 610, and 725 fix scalar equality and specify which ambiguous spellings to reject. The displayed admission predicate still evaluates `data/str-index-of` on a nullable namespace. An ordinary `:k` can therefore fail before admission completes. [String argument check](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc:281) |\n| #5 Verified export arity and role | `OPEN` | Lines 487–495 now establish guest lambda arity from verified UAST and require address-pinned accessor conformance. For hooks, the frontend table at line 338 supplies expected arity but no export-role binding. For host targets, the registry retains a profile **address**, while line 491 needs the profile’s `:yin.k/arities`. [UAST lambda shape](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc:35) · [Host registration](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:249) |\n| #6 Dependency pins, trailing forms, C1, and goldens | `CONFIRMED-FIXED` | Lines 265–266, 313, 795, and 803 specify the three emission choices independently. D4 authorizes regeneration when the tree or C1 table changes. This resolves the conflict between the existing Python trailing form and Clojure’s empty trailing vector. [Python emitter](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:4105) · [Clojure emitter](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:183) |\n| #7 Unit-owned ambient resolver | `CONFIRMED-FIXED` | Lines 441–445, 481–485, 623–625, and 635 carry the resolver into each unit’s fresh globals cell and preserve it across writes. Line 806 gates two units using the same `clj.py` address with different aliases. This supplies the unit-specific input missing in r4. [Live unit composition](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2519) |\n| #8 Cell predicates, compound ordering, and NaN | `CONFIRMED-FIXED` | Lines 709–715 exclude authenticated cells before collection classification. Lines 724–731 define nullable namespace ordering and within-kind vector, map, and set comparisons. Line 806 explicitly requires `[NaN] == [NaN]` to be false. [Retained collection predicates](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2743) · [String comparator](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc:396) |\n| #9 Python effect ceiling | `CONFIRMED-FIXED` | Lines 288 and 803 distinguish the proposed six-cell-effect `py` recipe with an empty trailing vector from recipes that execute `require` and incur `:module/require`. The example and P0 gate now agree. [Current Python trailing form](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:4112) · [Primitive effect](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:429) |\n\n**Earlier closures.** I found no reversal of the previously closed r1 **#2, #5, #8, #9, #10**, r2 **F2, F5, F6, F7, F8**, or r3 **#1, #2, #4, #10, #11, #12** in their original scope. The design retains frontend-owned lowering, open generator-frame dispatch, qualified frame reads, the integer refusal algebra, boxed float-policy boundaries, authenticated higher-order closure construction, explicit host limits, and the bare-`except:` and comprehension contracts. D4 deliberately supersedes the old byte-preservation criterion. The new P2/P3 issues below prevent a broader claim of runtime parity. [Control and numeric contracts](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:144) · [Admission](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:297) · [Phase gates](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:803)\n\n## 3. New or remaining findings\n\n| Severity | File:line | Invariant / evidence | Recommended correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **HIGH** | [yang.preludes.md:602](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:602) | An absent namespace is valid. The shown slash test passes `nil` to `data/str-index-of`, which requires a string. This affects ordinary unqualified keys and can also turn the promised `:unsupported-key` refusal for an ambiguous name into an operational error. [Primitive implementation](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc:281) | Guard all namespace string operations with a presence check. Always check the name. Gate successful insert and lookup for `:k` and `[:k]` alongside the ambiguous-identifier refusals. |\n| **HIGH** | [yang.preludes.md:491](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:491) | The listed checks admit `clj/prim-get` as a binary `:op/add` target on shape alone. The same issue applies to executable literal targets. On the host path, `register-host-module` discards the full profile record after recording its address and callable effects. [Frontend contract shape](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:338) · [Registry representation](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:253) | Bind conformance or frontend authorization to the exact module address, export, and role. For a host export, resolve and verify its full primitive profile by the registered address. Add a same-arity, wrong-role refusal. |\n| **HIGH** | [yang.preludes.md:510](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:510) | The mandatory `[body-fn ambient-resolver]` entry leaves PHP’s composition-supplied request, response, and diagnostic stream references without a specified path. Live lowering emits two or four operands. The runtime consumes the request to seed superglobals and emits on the supplied streams during execution. [PHP lowering](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3910) · [PHP entry](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5855) | Carry the resolver and sealed frontend-specific inputs in an explicit unit context, or specify a frontend-owned entry adapter that closes over them. Gate both PHP entry modes, including request-derived data and observable stream output. |\n| **HIGH** | [yang.preludes.md:734](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:734) | P3 removes `invoke-value` and the old `library-for` path. The proposed dispatcher admits only authenticated function cells. Native Clojure also invokes maps, vectors, keywords, and sets as data. An existing fixture requires a locally bound `{:k 9}` invoked with `:k` to return `9`. [Live dispatch](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1463) · [Collection semantics](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2626) · [Fixture](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/test/yang/clojure_test.clj:3197) | Give the unified native Clojure profile an explicit collection-invocation branch. Keep authenticated function admission for `yang.call` and preserve rejection of forged entries. Run the existing fixture in bundled and linked modes. |\n| **HIGH** | [yang.preludes.md:644](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:644) | The proof that `(fn [m k] (get m k))` reaches the primitive relies on an isolated **linked** module store. In a bundle, a source `defn get` writes `get` into the task store, which precedes primitives in lookup. The current preamble explicitly handles this case. The design specifies bundled protection for `yrt.escape` but leaves the new `clj` and `clojure.core.impl` bodies exposed. [Source definition emission](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:707) · [Existing protection](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2483) · [Lookup order](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:116) | Specify how bundled library bodies retain primitive bindings independently of source definitions. Gate a source-defined `get` and `assoc` followed by library lookup, insertion, and callable invocation in both modes. |\n| **HIGH** | [yang.preludes.md:313](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:313) | A verified dependency pin does not install a module in a task. The linker explicitly permits an absent deferred dependency. Today the linked Python wrapper requires `yang.call` and `py`; once `py` calls extracted `yrt.*` exports, the design needs to identify who installs them. Likewise, descriptor and runtime-profile addresses are pinned independently at lines 517–518. [Install contract](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1384) · [Live Python wrapper](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2533) · [Unit dependency declarations](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/yang/core/module.cljc:36) | Assign dependency-first installation to the linked composition entry point. Reconcile descriptor and runtime pins by module symbol, and declare direct module references emitted into each unit. Gate a cold task calling a transitive helper and a mismatched-address refusal. |\n| **MEDIUM** | [yang.preludes.md:601](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:601) | The key gate accepts every exact-integer carrier. On Node that includes both `Number(1)` and `BigInt(1)`. A host collection can distinguish them while `integer/compare` and Jing identify one integer. This also affects nested keys and lookup with a different carrier. [Accepted carriers](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/src/cljc/dao/host/integer.cljc:66) · [Jing identity fixture](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/test/dao/jing/cbor_content_equality_test.cljc:53) | Apply checked `integer/normalize` recursively before host-key insertion or lookup, or use a representation with the specified integer identity. Gate insertion with one carrier and lookup and replacement with the other. |\n| **MEDIUM** | [yang.preludes.md:623](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:623) | `:clj/unbound` represents a resolver miss and an uninitialized local, yet it is also a legal keyword value. A valid `:kind :value` projection of that keyword raises `NameError`. Assigning the same value to a local makes a later read appear unbound. [Projection contract](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:493) · [Admitted scalar values](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:605) | Represent presence separately from the payload for resolver results and local cells. Gate a projected `:clj/unbound`, a local holding it, and a genuinely absent name. |\n\n## 4. Owner decisions\n\n| Decision | Confirmation |\n|---|---|\n| **D1** | **A remains well framed.** Task-local lexical cells support reassignment and `nonlocal`. The local representation needs an independent bound state. |\n| **D2** | **A remains well framed.** `yrt.*` names linker modules and `yang.rt.*` names their implementation namespaces. |\n| **D3** | **A remains well framed.** Retain Python’s float tag through P1 and keep the CPython equality oracle at the language boundary. |\n| **D4** | **Settled by the owner.** Regenerate affected goldens per slice and judge correctness through behavioral, four-host, and language-oracle gates. |\n| **D5** | **A remains well framed.** Curated aliases, lexical precedence, and a unit-bound resolver support independent projections. The role and presence checks in §3 complete the admission contract. |\n| **D6** | **Settled by the owner.** Migrate `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` and the two-module standard library in P3. The native collection-call and bundled lookup findings belong in that single implementation. |\n| **D7** | **A remains well framed for P1.** Both `-raw` algorithms and their distinct `1.1 ** 6` bit patterns are explicit. Unifying them remains a separate owner choice. |\n\nThe roadmap reflects the requested symmetry: all four frontends become descriptor-driven in P2, Python targets Clojure semantics in P3, and P4 exercises the reverse `:yang.clojure/py-v1` profile. [Roadmap](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:805) · [Decision ledger](/home/sto/tmp/yang-preludes-r4-review/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:813)"}}
